1
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:17,851
A makeover project
for your most unhinged leftovers.

2
00:00:17,917 --> 00:00:21,454
The best chefs in Korea will
turn your fridge inside out.

3
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:23,323
The classy cooking show has returned.

4
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:26,426
<i>-Chef & My Fridge!</i>
<i>-My Fridge!</i>

5
00:00:28,261 --> 00:00:30,764
LET'S DO THIS

6
00:00:30,830 --> 00:00:34,567
-We're back.
-Recently, an elementary school student

7
00:00:34,634 --> 00:00:38,204
-sent a letter to our production crew.
-That's right.

8
00:00:38,271 --> 00:00:41,441
-I wonder what it's about.
-Let me read it to you for a second.

9
00:00:41,508 --> 00:00:44,644
"Dear the production crew
of <i>Chef & My Fridge.</i>"

10
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:46,312
"Thank you so much

11
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:49,816
for making such a fun program
like <i>Chef & My Fridge.</i>"

12
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:51,851
"I bought the gummies
with my pocket money."

13
00:00:51,918 --> 00:00:54,387
-Gummies?
-"Please enjoy them together."

14
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:57,223
"Sincerely, Kim Da-yul."

15
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:59,059
-Da-yul.
-Gummies?

16
00:01:00,326 --> 00:01:02,095
WITH GUMMIES
SHE BOUGHT WITH HER POCKET MONEY

17
00:01:02,162 --> 00:01:04,464
-They look good.
-They are.

18
00:01:04,531 --> 00:01:07,100
These are so precious.
Da-yul sent these to us,

19
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:09,135
so let's try one each.

20
00:01:09,202 --> 00:01:11,638
-I'll savor it.
-I should too.

21
00:01:11,704 --> 00:01:14,240
Gummies mean so much to kids.
She must really like us.

22
00:01:14,307 --> 00:01:15,241
There are lots.

23
00:01:15,308 --> 00:01:17,944
I'll give you the rest of the box.

24
00:01:18,611 --> 00:01:20,647
OH, NAM-NO…

25
00:01:21,681 --> 00:01:23,249
We're eating one each.

26
00:01:23,316 --> 00:01:26,719
On top of that,
Da-yul drew every one of us.

27
00:01:26,786 --> 00:01:28,221
DA-YUL DREW US?

28
00:01:28,288 --> 00:01:30,990
Yes, she drew us.

29
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:32,292
DREW EACH PERSON WITH LOVE

30
00:01:32,358 --> 00:01:34,260
<i>"Mr. Kim Sung-ju."</i>

31
00:01:34,327 --> 00:01:35,795
<i>"Mr. Ahn Jung-hwan."</i>

32
00:01:35,862 --> 00:01:38,531
She drew a microphone for me
and a soccer ball for Jung-hwan.

33
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:39,933
-She added details.
-Yes.

34
00:01:39,999 --> 00:01:42,702
Are those dumplings on your head?
How cute.

35
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:44,671
Nam-no's nose is shaped like a hog snout.

36
00:01:46,873 --> 00:01:49,142
-Why am I so big?
-Right.

37
00:01:49,209 --> 00:01:50,110
HIS BODY IS QUITE BIG…

38
00:01:50,176 --> 00:01:51,511
I look like a snowman.

39
00:01:51,578 --> 00:01:52,412
It's a work of art.

40
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:56,282
-At least I'm thinner than Nam-no.
-You have fried shrimp on your head.

41
00:01:56,349 --> 00:01:58,852
You're right.
She spotted everyone's characteristics.

42
00:01:58,918 --> 00:02:00,620
-Sung-jun's going, "Emergency."
-Emergency.

43
00:02:00,687 --> 00:02:02,422
She did a great job with these details.

44
00:02:02,489 --> 00:02:05,525
-I have the devil's tail.
-You have the devil's tail.

45
00:02:05,592 --> 00:02:07,727
Sam has sprouts on his head.

46
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:10,063
For his naturalism.

47
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:12,465
-Is that a strawberry on Jong-won?
-A strawberry.

48
00:02:12,532 --> 00:02:15,435
-A strawberry.
-For the strawberry prince.

49
00:02:15,502 --> 00:02:16,836
She watched every episode.

50
00:02:16,903 --> 00:02:19,839
-We have to give it our best.
-Yes, we have to try our hardest.

51
00:02:20,106 --> 00:02:22,208
THANK YOU FOR THE GUMMIES

52
00:02:22,275 --> 00:02:23,910
Wait, there was a PS.

53
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:26,713
"PS: Don't attack Chef Hyun-suk so much."

54
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,648
DA-YUL…

55
00:02:28,715 --> 00:02:31,784
-Don't attack him too much.
-I guess kids feel heartbroken to see it.

56
00:02:31,851 --> 00:02:34,087
Today, for Da-yul's sake,

57
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:36,823
-do not attack me at all.
-Excuse me.

58
00:02:36,890 --> 00:02:38,725
Is your grandson named Da-yul?

59
00:02:39,025 --> 00:02:40,827
DO NOT ATTACK MY GRANDPA
SINCERELY, GRANDSON

60
00:02:40,894 --> 00:02:43,062
-He can already draw like that?
-Da-yul is a Kim.

61
00:02:43,129 --> 00:02:44,898
Just like your son-in-law, right?

62
00:02:44,964 --> 00:02:46,466
You're right.

63
00:02:46,533 --> 00:02:47,901
He's growing way too fast.

64
00:02:47,967 --> 00:02:49,068
He can already write?

65
00:02:49,135 --> 00:02:50,270
So this is not your grandson?

66
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:51,938
-No?
-It's not.

67
00:02:52,005 --> 00:02:55,441
If you attack me,
you will be hurting Da-yul's feelings too.

68
00:02:55,508 --> 00:02:56,943
Are you going to hurt a child's--

69
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:58,444
I'm going to attack you.

70
00:02:58,511 --> 00:02:59,612
PUNISHED.

71
00:02:59,979 --> 00:03:01,948
LET'S ALL LISTEN TO DA-YUL TODAY

72
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:04,817
Again, for all our fans
who are giving us support,

73
00:03:04,884 --> 00:03:07,587
we are in business as usual.

74
00:03:07,654 --> 00:03:09,189
PLEASE DON'T WORRY

75
00:03:09,255 --> 00:03:10,657
-Yes.
-We're always open.

76
00:03:10,723 --> 00:03:13,893
It's time to meet today's fridge owners!

77
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,128
Come on out!

78
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:19,199
Who are they?

79
00:03:19,265 --> 00:03:21,734
Who are they?

80
00:03:21,801 --> 00:03:24,604
Please welcome
Cho Yeo-jeong and Ha Seok-jin.

81
00:03:24,671 --> 00:03:26,439
-Hello.
-Welcome.

82
00:03:26,806 --> 00:03:28,508
WELCOME

83
00:03:28,575 --> 00:03:29,776
Two very good-looking guests.

84
00:03:29,842 --> 00:03:31,277
They light up the studio.

85
00:03:31,344 --> 00:03:34,280
The heroine of the film <i>Parasite,</i>

86
00:03:34,347 --> 00:03:37,650
acknowledged for her talent
in Cannes and the Oscars.

87
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:39,485
Please welcome

88
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:42,255
the world-renowned actor, Cho Yeo-jeong!

89
00:03:42,322 --> 00:03:45,758
-Hello.
-It's great to see you.

90
00:03:45,825 --> 00:03:47,527
Her face is tinier than yours.

91
00:03:47,594 --> 00:03:48,962
Right? So tiny.

92
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:52,599
Now, as for this guy,

93
00:03:52,665 --> 00:03:53,666
he's a good student,

94
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,801
a good actor,

95
00:03:54,867 --> 00:03:56,269
and a funny TV personality too.

96
00:03:56,336 --> 00:03:58,037
The well-rounded "problematic" man
who can do anything.

97
00:03:58,104 --> 00:03:59,939
Please welcome actor Ha Seok-jin.

98
00:04:00,006 --> 00:04:02,709
-Ha Seok-jin!
-Welcome to the show.

99
00:04:02,775 --> 00:04:06,579
-You were here once before, right?
-Yes, 11 years ago.

100
00:04:06,646 --> 00:04:09,315
He has visited us once before,
11 years ago.

101
00:04:09,382 --> 00:04:11,618
Is this your first time, Yeo-jeong?

102
00:04:11,684 --> 00:04:13,386
I love to eat,

103
00:04:13,453 --> 00:04:15,288
so I always watched the show

104
00:04:15,355 --> 00:04:18,658
and wondered how good
the dishes they made would be.

105
00:04:18,725 --> 00:04:22,695
Was there anyone
you wanted to meet in person?

106
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:23,930
-I like them all.
-I'm sure.

107
00:04:23,997 --> 00:04:25,265
I really do.

108
00:04:25,331 --> 00:04:27,166
But Jong-won and Nam-no…

109
00:04:27,233 --> 00:04:29,135
-Hey!
-Whoa.

110
00:04:29,202 --> 00:04:30,503
YOU CAN HAVE ALL THESE

111
00:04:30,837 --> 00:04:32,305
ALL MY LOVE♥

112
00:04:32,372 --> 00:04:35,241
When he gives up food,
it means that he's that thrilled.

113
00:04:35,308 --> 00:04:37,343
-He gave me his all.
-He did.

114
00:04:37,410 --> 00:04:38,411
If he gave you his food,

115
00:04:38,478 --> 00:04:40,246
-it's like giving you his organs.
-You're right.

116
00:04:40,313 --> 00:04:42,749
-Thank you.
-I never share my food.

117
00:04:42,815 --> 00:04:45,051
-The two chefs are very different.
-Yes.

118
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:46,286
Chef Jong-won seems

119
00:04:46,352 --> 00:04:49,155
organized and nicely presented,

120
00:04:49,222 --> 00:04:53,226
-whereas he seems more free-spirited.
-Free-spirited.

121
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:54,427
Not neatly organized, right?

122
00:04:54,494 --> 00:04:55,728
GIGGLE

123
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:57,830
-The opposite.
-I didn't mean that.

124
00:04:58,197 --> 00:04:59,766
HER FAVORITES ON THE POLAR OPPOSITES

125
00:04:59,832 --> 00:05:03,770
-There's a reason why they visited us.
-What is it?

126
00:05:03,836 --> 00:05:05,171
-First, Seok-jin.
-Yes.

127
00:05:05,238 --> 00:05:07,607
I'm starring in a KBS drama

128
00:05:07,674 --> 00:05:09,776
-called <i>Love on the Menu.</i>
-<i>Love on the Menu.</i>

129
00:05:09,842 --> 00:05:12,378
I see. So someone's love is on the menu.

130
00:05:12,445 --> 00:05:14,347
And there, I'm playing an Italian chef.

131
00:05:14,414 --> 00:05:15,548
Really?

132
00:05:15,615 --> 00:05:19,619
I was hoping to learn a few things
about the career of a chef today.

133
00:05:19,686 --> 00:05:22,055
<i>The Affair Was Just the Beginning</i>

134
00:05:22,121 --> 00:05:24,157
-is the title of the show I star in.
-What was that?

135
00:05:24,223 --> 00:05:26,025
<i>The Affair Was Just the Beginning.</i>

136
00:05:26,092 --> 00:05:27,960
I'm already intrigued by the title.

137
00:05:28,027 --> 00:05:29,729
It must be about affairs.

138
00:05:29,796 --> 00:05:32,965
A NEW COUPLE MOVES IN NEXT DOOR

139
00:05:33,032 --> 00:05:34,701
So the affair was just the beginning.

140
00:05:34,767 --> 00:05:37,704
We have to resolve a much bigger case.

141
00:05:37,770 --> 00:05:39,939
<i>So we all come together like bowling pins,</i>

142
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:41,641
<i>and the story just unravels like crazy.</i>

143
00:05:41,708 --> 00:05:44,811
-A serial collision black comedy.
-It sounds fun.

144
00:05:44,877 --> 00:05:46,512
I heard you chose this project

145
00:05:46,579 --> 00:05:49,582
-because of Kim Hye-soo.
-Yes.

146
00:05:49,649 --> 00:05:53,986
When I was much younger,
we were both in <i>Royal Story: Jang Hui-bin.</i>

147
00:05:54,053 --> 00:05:55,922
I always wanted to work with her again…

148
00:05:55,988 --> 00:05:58,291
-I see.
-…and I didn't want to miss the chance.

149
00:05:58,358 --> 00:06:00,193
How many years has it been

150
00:06:00,259 --> 00:06:01,761
-before this reunion?
-About 23 years.

151
00:06:02,161 --> 00:06:04,464
IN 23 YEARS!

152
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:05,832
Were you a child actor back then?

153
00:06:05,898 --> 00:06:06,999
No.

154
00:06:07,066 --> 00:06:09,936
It would've been great
if I were that young now.

155
00:06:10,002 --> 00:06:11,971
-When you were an infant?
-She was ten.

156
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:14,140
-Were you in it as a baby?
-Thank you.

157
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:16,876
-What do you mean? She was in the womb.
-Is that right?

158
00:06:16,943 --> 00:06:17,777
WAVING IT OFF

159
00:06:18,010 --> 00:06:20,646
WE'RE SAYING THAT YOU LOOK VERY YOUNG

160
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:23,950
Yeo-jeong is the reason
why one of the chefs

161
00:06:24,016 --> 00:06:26,586
began to work even harder as a chef.

162
00:06:26,652 --> 00:06:28,154
-What?
-She made someone here go,

163
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:29,455
-"I'll try harder!"
-Really?

164
00:06:29,522 --> 00:06:31,290
"I'll be an even better chef."

165
00:06:31,357 --> 00:06:34,527
"I won't be a shame
if I ever get to meet her."

166
00:06:34,594 --> 00:06:35,828
-Someone was like that.
-Who?

167
00:06:35,895 --> 00:06:38,231
-Jong-won.
-Really?

168
00:06:38,297 --> 00:06:39,899
What's going on?

169
00:06:39,966 --> 00:06:41,434
That's supposed to be my thing.

170
00:06:41,501 --> 00:06:43,770
I really enjoyed watching <i>Parasite,</i>

171
00:06:43,836 --> 00:06:45,438
and at the Blue Dragon Film Awards,

172
00:06:45,505 --> 00:06:48,808
she said this as her acceptance speech
for the Best Actress Award.

173
00:06:48,875 --> 00:06:51,210
"Acting always feels like

174
00:06:51,277 --> 00:06:54,247
-a crush who can always leave me."
-I did.

175
00:06:54,313 --> 00:06:56,582
And you said
that actually became your motivation.

176
00:06:56,649 --> 00:06:58,351
I just got chills. You're right.

177
00:06:58,418 --> 00:07:01,687
Because even a great actor like her
felt that way about her career,

178
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:04,490
I felt vindicated
about the way I felt about cooking.

179
00:07:04,557 --> 00:07:08,094
This means Yeo-jeong
pretty much shaped Jong-won.

180
00:07:08,161 --> 00:07:12,198
She has a fair share in his career.

181
00:07:12,265 --> 00:07:14,667
That was quite moving. Not bad.

182
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:16,369
2ND WEEK OF SMILING FOR JONG-WON

183
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,438
He didn't make me laugh,
but that was moving.

184
00:07:18,504 --> 00:07:21,240
-That's what he does now.
-His word resonates.

185
00:07:21,307 --> 00:07:22,308
Personally,

186
00:07:22,375 --> 00:07:25,211
I want to mention
what you ate in <i>Parasite,</i>

187
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:27,680
<i>-Chapaguri.</i>
<i>-Yes.</i>

188
00:07:27,747 --> 00:07:30,583
-It was a huge hit. You have a share.
-Which is profoundly related to me.

189
00:07:30,650 --> 00:07:32,452
-Yes.
-From <i>Dad! Where Are We Going?</i>

190
00:07:32,518 --> 00:07:35,755
-I actually spread it to the world.
-You did.

191
00:07:35,822 --> 00:07:37,557
-Really?
-You did that.

192
00:07:37,623 --> 00:07:39,659
When I saw it on <i>Parasite,</i>

193
00:07:39,725 --> 00:07:42,695
I was like, "Whoa, Chapaguri.
That's my Director Bong."

194
00:07:42,762 --> 00:07:44,630
-And it was made with beef.
-Yes.

195
00:07:44,697 --> 00:07:46,632
My gosh.

196
00:07:46,699 --> 00:07:49,769
Director Bong, I inspired you.

197
00:07:50,169 --> 00:07:51,304
SMUG KIM

198
00:07:51,370 --> 00:07:53,806
Everyone wants credit for everything.

199
00:07:53,873 --> 00:07:56,742
-That's enough.
-All right.

200
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:59,479
-Don't try to take the credit.
-Come on, Director Bong.

201
00:07:59,545 --> 00:08:00,980
-Leave him alone now.
-Fine.

202
00:08:01,047 --> 00:08:03,549
-I do deserve some credit.
-All right.

203
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:05,751
SOMEONE GIVE HIM A TINY SHARE…

204
00:08:05,818 --> 00:08:07,286
Wasn't it delicious?

205
00:08:07,353 --> 00:08:09,555
-It was.
-Right?

206
00:08:09,622 --> 00:08:13,359
I rarely eat <i>ramyeon </i>with <i>jjajang</i> sauce,

207
00:08:13,426 --> 00:08:16,863
so I got to use the shoot
as an excuse to enjoy it very much.

208
00:08:16,929 --> 00:08:19,632
Thank you for enjoying the dish.

209
00:08:19,699 --> 00:08:22,768
One second.
We spotted something very important.

210
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:25,304
-What is it?
-So this was it.

211
00:08:25,371 --> 00:08:28,708
I was wondering
why these two visited us together,

212
00:08:28,774 --> 00:08:32,912
and the connection was the same numbers

213
00:08:32,979 --> 00:08:35,114
added at the end
of their social media account's handle.

214
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:36,849
Their handles both end

215
00:08:36,916 --> 00:08:40,686
-in 0210.
-February 10th.

216
00:08:41,254 --> 00:08:43,122
Seok-jin looks flustered.

217
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:44,857
-I got thirsty.
-He got thirsty.

218
00:08:44,924 --> 00:08:46,292
What's going on?

219
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:50,062
We were just chatting and catching up,
and he mentioned,

220
00:08:50,129 --> 00:08:54,233
"Yeo-jeong, we have the same birthday."

221
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,435
<i>-It's been so long.</i>
<i>-It has been.</i>

222
00:08:56,502 --> 00:08:57,470
<i>Has it been 15 years?</i>

223
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:58,638
<i>-No, 16.</i>
<i>-Wait, 16?</i>

224
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:00,439
<i>-We saw each other in 2010.</i>
<i>-Right, 2010.</i>

225
00:09:00,506 --> 00:09:03,242
<i>My birthday on the Lunar calendar</i>
<i>is the same as yours.</i>

226
00:09:03,309 --> 00:09:06,212
<i>So we found out and went,</i>
<i>"We were both born on February 10th."</i>

227
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:07,179
<i>Yes, right.</i>

228
00:09:07,246 --> 00:09:09,215
<i>-We have the same birthday.</i>
<i>-Yes.</i>

229
00:09:09,782 --> 00:09:11,817
I just heard it too.
We have the same birthday.

230
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:13,786
-The same birthday?
-February 10th?

231
00:09:13,853 --> 00:09:15,755
-February 10th.
-That's Sooyoung's birthday too.

232
00:09:16,088 --> 00:09:17,723
SOOYOUNG'S HUBBY, THIS ISN'T THE TIME…

233
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:20,593
Have you two worked
in a drama or a show together?

234
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:24,630
I always wanted to work with her
on a drama or a film,

235
00:09:24,697 --> 00:09:25,965
but I've never had the chance.

236
00:09:26,032 --> 00:09:29,335
-Someone may cast them after this episode.
-After the show airs.

237
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:31,203
They seem like a good match.

238
00:09:31,270 --> 00:09:33,339
They met by coincidence and found out

239
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:34,340
that they have the same birthday.

240
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:37,310
-Yes.
-And so their love story begins.

241
00:09:37,677 --> 00:09:39,679
WHIPPING UP A SCENARIO

242
00:09:39,745 --> 00:09:41,514
-You're writing the story?
-Yes.

243
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:43,349
And they'll eat Chapaguri together.

244
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:47,086
You're trying to get
too much credit for it.

245
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:49,522
HE'S JUST HAPPY

246
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:50,456
We meet and go,

247
00:09:50,523 --> 00:09:51,524
"Zero, two, one, zero?"

248
00:09:52,024 --> 00:09:53,092
IMPROVISED ACTING

249
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:55,428
That's nice. She has already started.

250
00:09:55,494 --> 00:09:56,362
Yes, that's good.

251
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:59,265
Do a scene
so we can use it for the preview.

252
00:10:00,232 --> 00:10:01,801
-Acting?
-"Zero, two, one, zero?"

253
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:03,869
Say, "Do you want a bowl of Chapaguri?"

254
00:10:04,170 --> 00:10:06,305
CHAPAGURI KEEPS COMING BACK

255
00:10:06,372 --> 00:10:08,074
Please do it for us.

256
00:10:08,774 --> 00:10:09,642
You're surprised.

257
00:10:09,709 --> 00:10:11,744
-Zero…
-Zero, two, one, zero?

258
00:10:13,512 --> 00:10:14,547
When's your birthday?

259
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:15,848
February 10th.

260
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:18,618
Do you like Chapaguri…

261
00:10:19,585 --> 00:10:21,754
Cut! Come on, Seok-jin!

262
00:10:21,821 --> 00:10:24,390
What's wrong? Why did you get nervous?

263
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:27,126
That's so not like you.

264
00:10:27,193 --> 00:10:29,128
Please focus, Seok-jin.

265
00:10:29,195 --> 00:10:31,697
Why are we eating Chapaguri
because of the same birthday?

266
00:10:32,031 --> 00:10:33,199
TOUGH TO GET INTO IT…

267
00:10:33,265 --> 00:10:35,101
I know but help me out here.

268
00:10:35,167 --> 00:10:37,036
You have to go with it as an actor.

269
00:10:37,103 --> 00:10:38,371
One more take.

270
00:10:38,437 --> 00:10:39,872
You're great, Yeo-jeong.

271
00:10:39,939 --> 00:10:41,741
-Action.
-This is rough.

272
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:43,109
Is it your birthday?

273
00:10:43,175 --> 00:10:44,477
Yes, wait, 0210?

274
00:10:45,578 --> 00:10:46,579
February 10th?

275
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:47,880
Yes, 0210.

276
00:10:47,947 --> 00:10:50,149
By any chance, do you like Chapaguri?

277
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:51,684
Yes.

278
00:10:51,751 --> 00:10:53,119
With sirloin on top?

279
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:55,721
-Strip loin.
-Strip loin?

280
00:10:55,788 --> 00:10:57,657
Cut! That was perfect!

281
00:10:58,024 --> 00:10:59,692
THERE'S OUR PREVIEW

282
00:10:59,992 --> 00:11:01,093
EXHAUSTED…

283
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:02,228
Let's move on.

284
00:11:02,294 --> 00:11:03,429
To the next scene.

285
00:11:03,496 --> 00:11:04,664
We're continuing?

286
00:11:04,730 --> 00:11:06,232
IS IT NOT OVER YET?

287
00:11:06,298 --> 00:11:07,366
That was a good take.

288
00:11:07,433 --> 00:11:09,368
Our next product placement
is this beverage.

289
00:11:09,435 --> 00:11:11,237
-Okay.
-The next product.

290
00:11:11,604 --> 00:11:13,639
IT HELPS OUT A LOT WITH THE PRODUCTION…

291
00:11:13,706 --> 00:11:16,175
-I apologize for asking to do that.
-We're sorry.

292
00:11:16,642 --> 00:11:19,211
THANK YOU FOR YOUR GREAT PERFORMANCES

293
00:11:19,278 --> 00:11:20,980
This is the 30th year

294
00:11:21,047 --> 00:11:24,850
-since Yeo-jeong's debut.
-Are you serious?

295
00:11:24,917 --> 00:11:26,218
When did she make her debut?

296
00:11:26,285 --> 00:11:28,320
She first debuted

297
00:11:28,387 --> 00:11:30,756
back in 1997 as a magazine model.

298
00:11:30,823 --> 00:11:32,425
-For <i>CeCi.</i>
<i>-CeCi.</i>

299
00:11:32,491 --> 00:11:33,626
How do you know?

300
00:11:33,693 --> 00:11:34,560
<i>CeCi?</i>

301
00:11:34,627 --> 00:11:36,328
I know what sassy is.

302
00:11:36,395 --> 00:11:38,964
Back then, there were <i>CeCi, KiKi,</i>
and <i>Fashionable Communication.</i>

303
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:41,867
-They were the big three.
-That's right.

304
00:11:41,934 --> 00:11:44,336
-Wasn't it <i>Sunday Seoul</i>?
-Back then…

305
00:11:44,403 --> 00:11:45,871
Chef Hyun-suk, for you,

306
00:11:45,938 --> 00:11:46,972
wasn't it <i>Sunday Seoul</i>?

307
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:49,141
EXACTLY WHAT HE EXPECTED…

308
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,209
LOL

309
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,546
Just now, he was saying,

310
00:11:53,612 --> 00:11:55,214
"Wasn't it <i>Sunday Seoul?"</i>

311
00:11:55,281 --> 00:11:56,849
Is that an ice cream brand?

312
00:11:56,916 --> 00:11:58,050
"Sunday" or "sundae"?

313
00:11:58,117 --> 00:12:01,220
There was this thick magazine
called <i>Sunday Seoul.</i>

314
00:12:01,287 --> 00:12:03,556
I remember CeCi. That was a big one.

315
00:12:03,622 --> 00:12:06,025
I was looking at it
and said, "Who is this?"

316
00:12:06,092 --> 00:12:07,960
She was so beautiful.

317
00:12:08,027 --> 00:12:09,729
Yeo-jeong

318
00:12:09,795 --> 00:12:12,264
was already a superstar
even in her kindergarten days.

319
00:12:12,331 --> 00:12:13,632
CHUCKLE

320
00:12:13,699 --> 00:12:14,734
We got a picture of her.

321
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,735
-Whoa.
-Let's take a look.

322
00:12:15,801 --> 00:12:17,269
-That's Yeo-jeong.
-Oh, no.

323
00:12:18,037 --> 00:12:19,772
-That's Yeo-jeong.
-Oh, no.

324
00:12:20,506 --> 00:12:23,142
-That was her in the kindergarten.
-She looks the same.

325
00:12:23,209 --> 00:12:25,544
-My gosh.
-How does she look that good?

326
00:12:25,611 --> 00:12:28,280
-Her pupils are so huge.
-She looks like a doll.

327
00:12:28,347 --> 00:12:29,648
Was that in your high school?

328
00:12:29,715 --> 00:12:32,384
-My high school graduation portrait.
-The graduation picture.

329
00:12:32,451 --> 00:12:35,921
What was it like when you were in school?
Just tell us the facts.

330
00:12:35,988 --> 00:12:39,091
I didn't know how popular I was.

331
00:12:39,325 --> 00:12:40,659
REALLY?

332
00:12:40,726 --> 00:12:42,828
My father was quite strict,

333
00:12:42,895 --> 00:12:45,397
so I had to go straight home after school.

334
00:12:45,464 --> 00:12:48,134
Did boys call you at home?

335
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:52,037
My older sister
was also famous for her looks,

336
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:54,240
so when someone would call us at night,

337
00:12:54,306 --> 00:12:56,442
my dad picked up.

338
00:12:56,509 --> 00:12:58,778
Most boys would just hang up, right?

339
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:02,114
Then he'd wake us both up to scold us.

340
00:13:02,181 --> 00:13:03,916
He couldn't tell who it was meant for.

341
00:13:03,983 --> 00:13:05,851
-"Why does he have your number?"
-Yes.

342
00:13:05,918 --> 00:13:07,119
"He has our home number?"

343
00:13:07,186 --> 00:13:09,455
I can tell by the look on Eun-yeong's face

344
00:13:09,522 --> 00:13:11,891
-that she can relate to her.
-Really?

345
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:14,059
-You're a twin.
-As someone who has a sister,

346
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:16,495
I can understand the difficulties

347
00:13:16,562 --> 00:13:18,130
your father went through.

348
00:13:18,197 --> 00:13:20,633
Because we were
the High Beams of Geumjeong-dong.

349
00:13:20,699 --> 00:13:22,034
-High Beams?
-High Beams?

350
00:13:22,101 --> 00:13:24,503
Whenever we showed up,

351
00:13:24,570 --> 00:13:26,972
people said we lit up the place.

352
00:13:27,039 --> 00:13:28,440
Because you're so gorgeous.

353
00:13:28,507 --> 00:13:30,609
Are you sure you weren't gangsters?
"The High Beams"?

354
00:13:30,676 --> 00:13:32,845
-She changed lanes without signaling.
-It means something else.

355
00:13:32,912 --> 00:13:34,547
THAT'S NOT IT

356
00:13:34,613 --> 00:13:36,148
-We were radiant.
-The radiance.

357
00:13:36,215 --> 00:13:38,384
Excuse me. Do you have proof?

358
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:40,820
I sent some to the writers.

359
00:13:40,886 --> 00:13:43,088
-Let's take a look.
-Let's do that.

360
00:13:43,155 --> 00:13:44,757
-Really?
-I'm serious.

361
00:13:44,824 --> 00:13:46,458
The High Beams of Geumjeong-dong.

362
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,562
-How cute.
-Whoa.

363
00:13:49,628 --> 00:13:52,965
-Is your sister on the right?
-Which one's your sister?

364
00:13:53,032 --> 00:13:56,168
I'm on the left,
the one giving femme fatale vibes.

365
00:13:56,235 --> 00:13:57,303
You're on the left?

366
00:13:57,369 --> 00:13:59,572
-Femme fatale?
-Femme fatale?

367
00:13:59,638 --> 00:14:01,207
She's missing a button.

368
00:14:01,273 --> 00:14:03,542
-You're right.
-The one in the middle.

369
00:14:03,609 --> 00:14:05,644
-She must've fought.
-It was taken after a fight.

370
00:14:05,711 --> 00:14:08,280
Her sister pulled out her button,

371
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:10,850
and Eun-yeong pulled out her hair.

372
00:14:10,916 --> 00:14:12,117
A MESS…

373
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:13,686
Yes, you two must've fought.

374
00:14:13,752 --> 00:14:15,888
-Yes, we didn't really get along.
-You didn't?

375
00:14:15,955 --> 00:14:17,389
One of the chefs

376
00:14:17,456 --> 00:14:19,959
wants to chime in
now that we're talking about looks.

377
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:20,960
What?

378
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:23,262
This one has a confession to make.

379
00:14:23,329 --> 00:14:25,598
-I'll read the transcript word for word.
-The transcript?

380
00:14:25,664 --> 00:14:28,601
"My looks
were actually surgically enhanced."

381
00:14:28,667 --> 00:14:29,902
Surgically enhanced?

382
00:14:29,969 --> 00:14:31,370
-Plastic surgery?
-A confession.

383
00:14:31,437 --> 00:14:32,638
Someone had work done?

384
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:33,839
Chef Hyun-suk?

385
00:14:33,906 --> 00:14:35,174
-What?
-Yes.

386
00:14:35,241 --> 00:14:36,075
-You got work done?
-You did?

387
00:14:36,141 --> 00:14:37,376
Where?

388
00:14:37,443 --> 00:14:39,812
I didn't say I had good looks,
that I did have work done.

389
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:42,147
-Like the High Beams of Geumjeong-dong…
-The High Beams.

390
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:44,650
…people used to have nicknames
with their neighborhood.

391
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:46,852
I was the Black Mantis of Geumho-dong.

392
00:14:47,353 --> 00:14:49,255
HOW FRIGHTENING…

393
00:14:49,321 --> 00:14:50,723
-Black Mantis?
-Black Mantis?

394
00:14:50,789 --> 00:14:53,492
I used to show martial arts forms
like the praying mantis pose.

395
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:56,562
Now, here's an important piece of fact.

396
00:14:56,629 --> 00:14:59,064
I had a black wart on my forehead
like a mantis's eyes.

397
00:15:00,532 --> 00:15:02,001
Hence, the Black Mantis.

398
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:03,302
What was his name?

399
00:15:03,369 --> 00:15:04,904
The guy who blows his nose.

400
00:15:04,970 --> 00:15:06,038
-Jung Dong-nam.
-Yes, Jung Dong-nam!

401
00:15:06,105 --> 00:15:08,674
Jung Dong-nam!

402
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:10,676
Can you use computer graphics on him?

403
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,645
TA-DA

404
00:15:12,978 --> 00:15:14,513
THAT LOOKS PERFECT

405
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:17,950
So I had it removed
with a laser procedure.

406
00:15:18,017 --> 00:15:19,585
You removed it completely.

407
00:15:19,652 --> 00:15:21,420
-And then, my nickname changed.
-To what?

408
00:15:21,487 --> 00:15:22,688
White Mantis?

409
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:23,923
Laser Choi.

410
00:15:23,989 --> 00:15:27,259
-Laser Choi?
-Laser Choi of Geumho-dong.

411
00:15:27,326 --> 00:15:28,427
Laser Choi.

412
00:15:28,494 --> 00:15:30,763
-I probably have photos from those days.
-Photos?

413
00:15:30,829 --> 00:15:33,632
-Did you turn those in?
-He did.

414
00:15:33,699 --> 00:15:35,834
I see. He turned those in,

415
00:15:35,901 --> 00:15:38,237
but they were pictures
after the procedure.

416
00:15:38,304 --> 00:15:39,939
His Laser Choi era?

417
00:15:40,005 --> 00:15:43,208
-Let's see it. Laser Choi of Geumho-dong.
-Let's see it.

418
00:15:43,275 --> 00:15:44,610
-What?
-Who is that?

419
00:15:44,677 --> 00:15:47,246
Is that a wart in the left photo?

420
00:15:47,313 --> 00:15:49,148
You had a mole on your left cheek.

421
00:15:49,214 --> 00:15:50,916
You had a wart on your cheek too?

422
00:15:51,483 --> 00:15:53,919
-No, it was a mole.
-A mole.

423
00:15:53,986 --> 00:15:55,054
You had a mole there?

424
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:59,091
That was the second procedure.
I'm highly lasered.

425
00:15:59,725 --> 00:16:00,559
"High Laser."

426
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:02,628
Hyun-suk's looks
turned out to be surgically enhanced.

427
00:16:02,695 --> 00:16:03,996
That's cool.

428
00:16:04,063 --> 00:16:07,399
As you have seen
in Yeo-jeong's high school picture,

429
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:10,769
she still looks as youthful
as she did back then,

430
00:16:10,836 --> 00:16:12,338
-leaving many curious.
-I'm curious.

431
00:16:12,404 --> 00:16:14,673
What she always mentions is working out.

432
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:16,175
What do you do?

433
00:16:16,241 --> 00:16:18,544
I always tell myself
to work out at least once a day.

434
00:16:18,610 --> 00:16:22,381
I go to a modern dance studio
that I've been a member of for a while.

435
00:16:22,448 --> 00:16:25,884
Or when the weather is nice,
I jog or go swimming.

436
00:16:25,951 --> 00:16:28,187
-She works out a lot.
-So one of the three.

437
00:16:28,253 --> 00:16:31,523
She stays disciplined
and works out a lot too.

438
00:16:31,590 --> 00:16:34,660
I wonder what she keeps in her fridge.

439
00:16:35,627 --> 00:16:38,464
-It's nerve-racking.
-I'm looking forward to it.

440
00:16:38,530 --> 00:16:40,299
All my friends laughed at me

441
00:16:40,366 --> 00:16:42,167
when I told them I'd be on the show.

442
00:16:42,234 --> 00:16:43,502
They know what my fridge is like.

443
00:16:43,569 --> 00:16:45,504
"Can they cook
with just carbonated water?"

444
00:16:46,271 --> 00:16:47,239
Carbonated water?

445
00:16:47,306 --> 00:16:50,542
They laughed at me saying,
"What can they make with club soda?"

446
00:16:51,443 --> 00:16:54,279
Let's find out what Yeo-jeong eats.

447
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:56,415
-We present Yeo-jeong's fridge.
-Fridge.

448
00:16:57,082 --> 00:16:58,817
-She doesn't have much.
-Wait. Emergency.

449
00:16:58,884 --> 00:17:00,552
-It's too empty, right?
-Right.

450
00:17:00,619 --> 00:17:04,289
She doesn't keep
a whole lot of food at home.

451
00:17:04,356 --> 00:17:07,626
First of all, the top shelf

452
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:10,329
-has probiotics.
-Probiotics.

453
00:17:10,396 --> 00:17:13,932
I take one on an empty stomach
with cold water in the morning.

454
00:17:13,999 --> 00:17:16,135
I put it where I can see it
to make sure I remember.

455
00:17:17,236 --> 00:17:18,704
How do you eat your breakfast?

456
00:17:18,771 --> 00:17:21,407
I only eat blueberries for breakfast.

457
00:17:21,473 --> 00:17:22,674
-Blueberries.
-Yes.

458
00:17:22,741 --> 00:17:24,877
-Blueberries and…
-I see them here.

459
00:17:24,943 --> 00:17:26,445
-These.
-Just these?

460
00:17:26,512 --> 00:17:28,313
But I wanted something more,

461
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:31,850
so I add some ricotta
and agave syrup to them.

462
00:17:31,917 --> 00:17:33,252
That sounds delicious.

463
00:17:33,318 --> 00:17:35,521
People often eat those with yogurt.

464
00:17:35,587 --> 00:17:38,323
My body doesn't take dairy products well.

465
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:40,259
-Lactose intolerance?
-Yes.

466
00:17:40,325 --> 00:17:42,194
But I love dairy products.

467
00:17:42,261 --> 00:17:44,663
When I tried ricotta,

468
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:48,100
I guess something about it
worked with me and it wasn't as bad.

469
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:51,303
That's why
I've substituted it for ricotta.

470
00:17:52,504 --> 00:17:54,440
Actually, I used to eat

471
00:17:54,506 --> 00:17:58,277
things like mugwort <i>tteok</i> for breakfast
because I love <i>tteok,</i> rice cake.

472
00:17:58,343 --> 00:18:02,114
But then I wanted to reduce
my calorie intake even by a little,

473
00:18:02,181 --> 00:18:03,549
so I've opted for blueberries.

474
00:18:03,615 --> 00:18:04,583
FOR HER DIET

475
00:18:04,650 --> 00:18:06,618
Then I wanted to cut down on sugar,

476
00:18:06,685 --> 00:18:08,287
so it's now ricotta and olive oil.

477
00:18:08,353 --> 00:18:10,222
Ricotta and olive oil?

478
00:18:10,289 --> 00:18:12,291
You seem to care
about your glucose intake.

479
00:18:12,357 --> 00:18:13,592
Because I have a sweet tooth.

480
00:18:13,659 --> 00:18:15,427
-You have a sweet tooth?
-To cut back.

481
00:18:15,494 --> 00:18:17,029
I love things like cake

482
00:18:17,096 --> 00:18:18,130
or donuts.

483
00:18:18,197 --> 00:18:20,699
-I love them.
-So you have a sweet tooth.

484
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:24,269
And on this side,
something's written on the bag.

485
00:18:24,336 --> 00:18:25,871
"Toasted buckwheat."

486
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:28,640
"You may infuse them in hot or cold water,

487
00:18:28,707 --> 00:18:30,876
or you can even pop them in like nuts."

488
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:32,711
"Buckwheat tea, 80 grams, 3,000 won."

489
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,580
I love buckwheat noodles,

490
00:18:34,646 --> 00:18:38,984
so I even go on tours to find
good soba or buckwheat noodle places.

491
00:18:39,051 --> 00:18:40,085
Soba.

492
00:18:40,152 --> 00:18:43,322
So I often order
buckwheat noodles from various places,

493
00:18:43,388 --> 00:18:44,756
and some restaurants

494
00:18:44,823 --> 00:18:47,659
give toasted buckwheat out to customers.

495
00:18:47,726 --> 00:18:51,096
I like to have it
as hot buckwheat tea in the morning,

496
00:18:51,163 --> 00:18:55,033
and I even sprinkle some
on chocolate to make it crunchy.

497
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:56,502
It adds a nice bite to it.

498
00:18:56,568 --> 00:18:57,870
Yes, it's deliciously nutty.

499
00:18:57,936 --> 00:19:00,506
Try having it with <i>dak-galbi,</i>
spicy stir-fried chicken.

500
00:19:00,572 --> 00:19:02,107
-Whoa.
-It's so good.

501
00:19:02,174 --> 00:19:04,843
It'll feel like fried chicken, right?

502
00:19:04,910 --> 00:19:06,979
We usually order fried chicken, don't we?

503
00:19:07,045 --> 00:19:11,083
But if you dip <i>dak-galbi </i>in buckwheat,
it'll feel like that crispy skin.

504
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,352
It must be crispy. That sounds good.

505
00:19:13,418 --> 00:19:15,320
What's this white powder?

506
00:19:15,387 --> 00:19:18,423
-Buckwheat flour.
-Does it work well with your body?

507
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,159
Yes, I think so.

508
00:19:20,225 --> 00:19:21,560
-And you like it too.
-Very much.

509
00:19:21,627 --> 00:19:24,096
What can you not eat, then? First, milk.

510
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:25,831
-Not many dairy products.
-No dairy products.

511
00:19:25,898 --> 00:19:27,833
-And?
-I feel bad for the chefs

512
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:29,101
because I have no meat.

513
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:31,270
-Not in my fridge.
-No meat?

514
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:33,105
-Whoa. An emergency.
-That's a first.

515
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:35,007
-No meat?
-She has no meat.

516
00:19:35,073 --> 00:19:36,708
-She doesn't.
-A fridge without meat.

517
00:19:36,775 --> 00:19:38,377
-This is bad.
-There's no meat.

518
00:19:38,443 --> 00:19:39,578
I do like it,

519
00:19:39,645 --> 00:19:42,481
but it takes a toll on my body
if I eat it too often.

520
00:19:42,548 --> 00:19:43,982
-It doesn't work with her.
-I guess not.

521
00:19:44,049 --> 00:19:45,551
Warming foods don't work well with me,

522
00:19:45,617 --> 00:19:47,252
so I have
no garlic or onion either. Sorry.

523
00:19:47,319 --> 00:19:48,487
Because of your constitution.

524
00:19:48,554 --> 00:19:49,922
-No garlic, no onion.
-No onion?

525
00:19:49,988 --> 00:19:52,624
-That's why you eat buckwheat.
-It cools your body.

526
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:55,627
-Cooling food for your hot constitution.
-That's right.

527
00:19:55,694 --> 00:19:57,396
-What's this?
-Mung beans.

528
00:19:57,462 --> 00:19:58,964
-Mung beans.
-Yes.

529
00:19:59,031 --> 00:20:01,934
-How do you eat that?
-I like mung beans,

530
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:02,834
so I boil them

531
00:20:03,902 --> 00:20:05,871
and eat them with fried eggs,

532
00:20:05,938 --> 00:20:08,407
mixed with soy sauce.

533
00:20:08,473 --> 00:20:12,077
What about when you feel like
letting loose and binge-eating?

534
00:20:12,144 --> 00:20:13,545
-I eat lots.
-What do you eat?

535
00:20:13,612 --> 00:20:14,846
So that does happen?

536
00:20:14,913 --> 00:20:16,448
<i>Jjajangmyeon. Ramyeon.</i>

537
00:20:16,515 --> 00:20:18,217
Pizza. I love all those.

538
00:20:18,283 --> 00:20:19,418
-I see.
-Carbs.

539
00:20:19,484 --> 00:20:22,521
I try to eat <i>jjajangmyeon</i>
and <i>ramyeon</i> only once a year.

540
00:20:22,588 --> 00:20:24,356
-What?
-Once a year?

541
00:20:24,423 --> 00:20:26,225
I can never live like that.

542
00:20:26,291 --> 00:20:29,595
-Only once a year?
-Like a health checkup, once a year.

543
00:20:29,661 --> 00:20:31,430
-Is it self-control?
-I decided to do that.

544
00:20:31,496 --> 00:20:32,664
But starting last year,

545
00:20:32,731 --> 00:20:34,833
I began to think, "Must I live like this?"

546
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,034
Exactly.

547
00:20:36,101 --> 00:20:37,436
So maybe twice a year each.

548
00:20:37,502 --> 00:20:38,637
-Twice a year.
-Wait.

549
00:20:38,704 --> 00:20:41,073
My hands literally shake when I eat those.

550
00:20:42,474 --> 00:20:44,243
-You must be sad afterward.
-It must be so dear.

551
00:20:44,309 --> 00:20:45,611
I'm already sad while eating.

552
00:20:45,677 --> 00:20:47,546
-It disappears.
-It's slowly disappearing.

553
00:20:47,613 --> 00:20:49,514
It's such a shame to see it disappear

554
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:50,616
-as I eat it.
-Twice a year.

555
00:20:50,682 --> 00:20:51,650
BOOHOO…

556
00:20:51,717 --> 00:20:53,385
What kind of pizza do you like?

557
00:20:53,452 --> 00:20:54,653
I like all kinds.

558
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,255
I still eat pizza from time to time.

559
00:20:57,389 --> 00:20:59,958
It's too heartbreaking
to hold back on pizza, so I just eat it.

560
00:21:00,025 --> 00:21:03,895
I like Italian pizza,
American pizza, Chicago pizza,

561
00:21:03,962 --> 00:21:05,864
and even Korean-style.

562
00:21:05,931 --> 00:21:07,432
So all kinds of pizza.

563
00:21:07,499 --> 00:21:10,469
If she tries that hard to stay in shape,

564
00:21:10,535 --> 00:21:12,638
-should they make healthy, low-calorie--
-No!

565
00:21:13,005 --> 00:21:14,139
SO URGENT

566
00:21:14,206 --> 00:21:15,474
-No.
-No?

567
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:16,675
-No.
-Not necessary?

568
00:21:16,742 --> 00:21:19,211
I came here today

569
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:22,547
-to treat myself.
-A delicious dish.

570
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:24,783
I'll gladly accept high-calorie dishes.

571
00:21:24,850 --> 00:21:28,287
-She'll gladly accept high-calorie dishes.
-Even desserts.

572
00:21:28,353 --> 00:21:29,855
The shelf below

573
00:21:29,921 --> 00:21:31,423
has some condiments.

574
00:21:31,490 --> 00:21:33,258
-Gochujang.
-Traditional gochujang.

575
00:21:33,325 --> 00:21:34,459
Do you enjoy Korean food?

576
00:21:34,526 --> 00:21:36,228
I love it.

577
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:38,397
-Especially <i>jeotgal,</i> salted seafood.
<i>-Jeotgal.</i>

578
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:41,733
Don't people usually eat this
with carbs like rice?

579
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:45,103
Yes, so my friends tease me
and call this bizarre.

580
00:21:45,170 --> 00:21:47,005
These days, there are breads

581
00:21:47,072 --> 00:21:49,508
made with rice, not flour.

582
00:21:49,574 --> 00:21:52,978
So I make a sandwich
and eat <i>jeotgal </i>as a side dish.

583
00:21:53,045 --> 00:21:54,613
-To eliminate the greasiness.
-Rice bread.

584
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:56,148
Some vegetables.

585
00:21:56,214 --> 00:21:59,084
Cucumber, celery, cilantro,

586
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:01,853
<i>chamnamul,</i> bracken, and cabbage.

587
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,889
You must like fruit.

588
00:22:03,955 --> 00:22:07,059
-Yes, like peaches, cherries, and plums.
-Peaches, plums.

589
00:22:07,125 --> 00:22:09,394
-Cherries.
-And figs.

590
00:22:09,461 --> 00:22:12,531
-I like seasonal fruit, like peaches now.
-Seasonal fruit.

591
00:22:12,597 --> 00:22:14,099
She likes seasonal fruit.

592
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:16,001
On this side,

593
00:22:16,068 --> 00:22:18,670
-pomegranate vinegar and <i>omija cheong.</i>
-She has lots of <i>cheong.</i>

594
00:22:18,737 --> 00:22:21,006
I see some vinegar
and similar things here.

595
00:22:21,073 --> 00:22:23,241
This was the first time I realized

596
00:22:23,308 --> 00:22:26,244
I had so many kinds of vinegar
in my fridge.

597
00:22:26,311 --> 00:22:27,913
I like that sour note.

598
00:22:27,979 --> 00:22:29,448
-You like sourness.
-Yes.

599
00:22:29,514 --> 00:22:31,149
I take those in various ways.

600
00:22:31,216 --> 00:22:33,151
As for the pomegranate vinegar
and lemon vinegar,

601
00:22:33,218 --> 00:22:34,853
I drink it when I crave beer

602
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:38,223
-by mixing club soda with <i>cheong.</i>
-By mixing it.

603
00:22:38,290 --> 00:22:41,126
And I enjoy it while watching a movie.
It's a beer substitute.

604
00:22:41,193 --> 00:22:44,529
You already have some beer.
Is it necessary to make that?

605
00:22:44,596 --> 00:22:46,131
Those are for guests.

606
00:22:47,366 --> 00:22:48,700
You don't drink it yourself?

607
00:22:48,767 --> 00:22:49,935
May I take some?

608
00:22:50,502 --> 00:22:54,172
She serves it to her guests
when she invites them over.

609
00:22:54,239 --> 00:22:55,507
We're her guests now.

610
00:22:55,774 --> 00:22:56,808
GIGGLING

611
00:22:56,875 --> 00:22:58,677
-For your house guests.
-Yes.

612
00:22:58,744 --> 00:23:01,213
-What are those laundry soap shapes?
-Laundry soap?

613
00:23:01,279 --> 00:23:03,215
-Laundry soap? These?
-Yes.

614
00:23:03,281 --> 00:23:05,283
Those are cookies I got as a present.

615
00:23:05,350 --> 00:23:06,451
-Cookies.
-Yes.

616
00:23:06,518 --> 00:23:08,754
Why would she keep
laundry soap in the fridge?

617
00:23:09,087 --> 00:23:10,722
SILENT…

618
00:23:10,789 --> 00:23:13,925
-He's old enough to remember soaps.
-Are you

619
00:23:13,992 --> 00:23:15,761
trying to hurt Da-yul?

620
00:23:15,827 --> 00:23:18,397
Why would she keep laundry soap in here?

621
00:23:18,463 --> 00:23:20,499
He used to do the laundry out by a stream.

622
00:23:20,565 --> 00:23:22,701
-Out by a stream?
-A stream?

623
00:23:22,768 --> 00:23:24,936
BACK IN THE DAY…

624
00:23:25,003 --> 00:23:27,906
What's this next to the beer?

625
00:23:27,973 --> 00:23:31,610
-It's trouble. I've never opened it.
-What is it?

626
00:23:31,676 --> 00:23:33,178
"Wolfgang Puck"?

627
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:35,714
-Wolfgang Puck is a chef.
-The steak house.

628
00:23:35,781 --> 00:23:37,048
Back in 2020

629
00:23:37,115 --> 00:23:39,918
<i>when I went to the Academy Awards,</i>

630
00:23:39,985 --> 00:23:44,322
that was probably a souvenir
given out to everyone attending.

631
00:23:44,389 --> 00:23:45,991
-It's probably chocolate.
-Chocolate.

632
00:23:46,057 --> 00:23:47,359
May we open it?

633
00:23:47,426 --> 00:23:48,393
Sure.

634
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:53,298
-The chocolate for the Oscar attendees.
-It's gold.

635
00:23:53,365 --> 00:23:54,433
Has it been six years?

636
00:23:54,499 --> 00:23:56,234
-It's shaped like the statuette.
-How cool.

637
00:23:56,301 --> 00:23:57,969
It's such a shame to eat it.

638
00:23:58,036 --> 00:23:59,237
I wouldn't be able to.

639
00:23:59,304 --> 00:24:02,274
-So only the attendees got these?
-Yes.

640
00:24:02,340 --> 00:24:04,810
I'll put it back in the fridge.

641
00:24:04,876 --> 00:24:07,212
Let's check out the freezer.

642
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:08,880
I see some seafood.

643
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:11,082
-Shrimp. Mackerel.
-Mackerel.

644
00:24:11,149 --> 00:24:12,951
-Squid. Octopus.
-She has lots of seafood.

645
00:24:13,218 --> 00:24:15,187
FULL OF SEAFOOD

646
00:24:15,253 --> 00:24:18,990
Seafood tends to be my main ingredient.

647
00:24:19,057 --> 00:24:20,192
She doesn't eat meat.

648
00:24:20,258 --> 00:24:21,359
-No.
-Does it work with you?

649
00:24:21,426 --> 00:24:23,361
Yes, I like seafood.

650
00:24:23,428 --> 00:24:25,730
How do you eat this octopus?

651
00:24:25,797 --> 00:24:29,701
That's one of the reasons why I came.

652
00:24:29,768 --> 00:24:31,703
I really like octopus,

653
00:24:31,770 --> 00:24:34,439
-but it's hard to work with.
-It's tough to cook octopus.

654
00:24:34,506 --> 00:24:36,274
So I wanted to ask you

655
00:24:36,341 --> 00:24:39,778
for tips on how to eat octopus.

656
00:24:39,845 --> 00:24:43,548
You should either cook it
for a very long time or very briefly.

657
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:44,716
-Either one.
-Really?

658
00:24:44,783 --> 00:24:45,684
I SEE

659
00:24:45,750 --> 00:24:47,519
Please use this octopus.

660
00:24:47,586 --> 00:24:49,354
That was her constitution-friendly fridge,

661
00:24:49,421 --> 00:24:51,356
and we're done looking through.

662
00:24:52,224 --> 00:24:54,059
Everything is constitution-friendly.

663
00:24:54,726 --> 00:24:57,796
Then what is she hoping to eat today?

664
00:24:57,863 --> 00:25:00,031
Let's find out her orders.

665
00:25:00,098 --> 00:25:01,099
Show us.

666
00:25:02,501 --> 00:25:05,370
Yeo-jeong's Constitution-Friendly Journey.

667
00:25:05,437 --> 00:25:07,205
How cool. Her name sounds like "journey."

668
00:25:07,272 --> 00:25:09,608
-She sticks to the constitutional diet.
-What I eat

669
00:25:09,674 --> 00:25:13,645
consists of usual ingredients
prepared in the same way.

670
00:25:13,712 --> 00:25:17,115
I wanted to try delicious dishes made with
ingredients friendly to my constitution.

671
00:25:17,182 --> 00:25:18,850
-That's it.
-I wanted to see how it goes.

672
00:25:18,917 --> 00:25:20,919
All right. What's the second order?

673
00:25:20,986 --> 00:25:22,087
The second one.

674
00:25:22,821 --> 00:25:25,557
Self-Discipline Was Just the Beginning.

675
00:25:26,258 --> 00:25:27,592
Then what's next?

676
00:25:27,659 --> 00:25:28,994
Was that just the beginning?

677
00:25:29,060 --> 00:25:32,931
I don't think self-discipline matters
on a day like this.

678
00:25:32,998 --> 00:25:35,534
I don't care if it's high in calories.

679
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:38,503
I'll consider this my cheat day
and eat something really good.

680
00:25:38,570 --> 00:25:39,804
All right.

681
00:25:39,871 --> 00:25:41,339
She disclosed both her orders.

682
00:25:41,406 --> 00:25:44,543
Take a look at the orders
and choose to participate.

683
00:25:44,609 --> 00:25:45,443
I'll go.

684
00:25:46,077 --> 00:25:49,080
Self-discipline
hasn't even begun in my life,

685
00:25:49,147 --> 00:25:51,583
which you can probably tell by my shape.

686
00:25:51,650 --> 00:25:53,585
I'll go for the second order…

687
00:25:53,652 --> 00:25:55,320
Stop touching.

688
00:25:55,387 --> 00:25:58,657
-I'll go for the second one.
-Self-Discipline Was Just the Beginning.

689
00:25:58,723 --> 00:26:00,025
All right. Good call.

690
00:26:00,091 --> 00:26:01,826
-He took a spot.
-Challenge your mortal enemy.

691
00:26:01,893 --> 00:26:03,695
No, I'd never take that spot.

692
00:26:04,362 --> 00:26:05,830
-I'll go.
-Ho-young?

693
00:26:06,131 --> 00:26:07,632
WHICH ONE?

694
00:26:07,699 --> 00:26:11,469
-Self-Discipline Was Just the Beginning.
-Really?

695
00:26:11,536 --> 00:26:14,806
I'll show you
what I had to do to turn out like me.

696
00:26:14,873 --> 00:26:16,841
I don't think she'd want that though.

697
00:26:16,908 --> 00:26:20,879
Poong and Ho-young will fight in the round
Self-Discipline Was Just the Beginning.

698
00:26:20,946 --> 00:26:22,714
WOW♥

699
00:26:22,781 --> 00:26:25,016
Someone must take
her constitution-friendly journey.

700
00:26:25,083 --> 00:26:26,518
Any volunteers?

701
00:26:26,585 --> 00:26:28,420
-I knew it.
-Of course.

702
00:26:28,486 --> 00:26:29,854
I saw in her fridge

703
00:26:29,921 --> 00:26:34,292
that she had many ingredients
I also liked, so I'll cook with those.

704
00:26:34,359 --> 00:26:36,528
He'll join your journey.

705
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:37,996
We need one more.

706
00:26:38,063 --> 00:26:39,397
Then I'll go.

707
00:26:39,464 --> 00:26:40,865
-Hey.
-Wait.

708
00:26:40,932 --> 00:26:43,168
-Did you read that right?
-He read it wrong again.

709
00:26:43,234 --> 00:26:46,371
She's not asking you
to keep your constitution as is.

710
00:26:46,438 --> 00:26:47,472
It's not my constitution?

711
00:26:47,539 --> 00:26:48,440
Not the greater Yang type.

712
00:26:48,506 --> 00:26:49,641
OH, IS THAT SO?

713
00:26:49,708 --> 00:26:51,109
Are you in, Nam-no?

714
00:26:51,176 --> 00:26:53,378
She showed me a bit of favor,

715
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:55,947
-so I want to cook for her.
-All right.

716
00:26:56,014 --> 00:26:58,183
-He's in.
-Thank you.

717
00:26:58,249 --> 00:27:00,418
Everything has been decided.

718
00:27:00,485 --> 00:27:03,321
So let us begin
Jong-won and Nam-no's round!

719
00:27:06,091 --> 00:27:10,295
<i>This is the first round of cook-off</i>
<i>with Yeo-jeong's ingredients.</i>

720
00:27:10,362 --> 00:27:13,131
Two of her favorite chefs
are up against each other.

721
00:27:13,198 --> 00:27:15,867
The organized one, Chef Son Jong-won,

722
00:27:16,434 --> 00:27:20,805
versus the messy one, Chef Yoon Nam-no.

723
00:27:20,872 --> 00:27:22,540
Can we consider

724
00:27:22,607 --> 00:27:25,677
the winner of this round your bias?

725
00:27:25,744 --> 00:27:26,578
-Sure.
-Okay.

726
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:28,913
-It won't be easy.
-Yes, of course.

727
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:30,415
The thing is, even after combining

728
00:27:30,482 --> 00:27:32,283
last year and this year's result,

729
00:27:32,350 --> 00:27:35,153
Jong-won has never lost once
against Nam-no.

730
00:27:35,220 --> 00:27:37,322
-He won all rounds.
-So far.

731
00:27:37,389 --> 00:27:41,192
The topic for this round
is a constitution-friendly diet.

732
00:27:41,259 --> 00:27:42,961
Out of concern,

733
00:27:43,028 --> 00:27:45,063
let me ask one question to Nam-no
before we begin.

734
00:27:45,130 --> 00:27:47,666
What's Yeo-jeong's body constitution?
She had mentioned it earlier.

735
00:27:47,732 --> 00:27:49,267
Tell me.

736
00:27:49,334 --> 00:27:50,502
She has a colder body.

737
00:27:50,568 --> 00:27:52,570
-"Colder body"?
-You're wrong.

738
00:27:52,637 --> 00:27:55,306
-It's the opposite.
-She has a naturally hot constitution.

739
00:27:55,373 --> 00:27:56,374
She has internal heat.

740
00:27:56,441 --> 00:27:58,710
She has a hotter body,
so she eats food that cools it down.

741
00:27:58,777 --> 00:28:00,779
I understood.

742
00:28:00,845 --> 00:28:02,580
Which ingredients does she like?

743
00:28:02,647 --> 00:28:05,050
-Buckwheat.
-Yes.

744
00:28:05,116 --> 00:28:07,786
-And no dairy products.
-That's correct.

745
00:28:07,852 --> 00:28:10,321
-She prefers seafood, no meat.
-Yes.

746
00:28:10,388 --> 00:28:11,623
You're right.

747
00:28:11,690 --> 00:28:12,957
He remembered it well.

748
00:28:13,024 --> 00:28:14,292
FEELING PROUD

749
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:16,995
Jong-won, you also eat <i>ramyeon</i>
only once a year?

750
00:28:17,662 --> 00:28:20,699
Yes, I also eat <i>ramyeon</i>
around once a year.

751
00:28:20,765 --> 00:28:23,034
I haven't had it this year,
and I really get you.

752
00:28:23,635 --> 00:28:25,203
-He'll have it later this year.
-You understand her.

753
00:28:25,270 --> 00:28:26,571
Another thing I connected with

754
00:28:26,638 --> 00:28:28,873
was that I also drink club soda
when I crave spicy food.

755
00:28:30,575 --> 00:28:32,410
-You do?
-When I'm stressed out.

756
00:28:32,477 --> 00:28:35,513
When I'm bored,
I drink club soda with lemon flavoring.

757
00:28:35,814 --> 00:28:37,482
FEELING DISTANT…

758
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:40,151
And that's his off day.

759
00:28:40,218 --> 00:28:42,087
-He's like me.
-He's very disciplined.

760
00:28:42,921 --> 00:28:44,723
CHEF NAM-NO'S INGREDIENTS:
TOASTED BUCKWHEAT, BUCKWHEAT FLOUR

761
00:28:44,789 --> 00:28:47,092
MUNG BEAN, CHICKPEA, CORN, SHRIMP, SQUID
POLLACK ROE, MUGWORT TTEOK, AND MORE

762
00:28:47,158 --> 00:28:49,928
Chef Nam-no, what are you making?

763
00:28:49,994 --> 00:28:51,663
I'm making

764
00:28:51,730 --> 00:28:55,266
Will Win a Star With Buckwheat.

765
00:28:55,333 --> 00:28:56,768
Will Win a Star.

766
00:28:56,835 --> 00:28:58,536
-Will Win a Star.
-You have a dialect.

767
00:28:58,603 --> 00:29:00,605
-Will Win a Star.
-Yes.

768
00:29:00,672 --> 00:29:02,774
The Gangwon-do dialect.

769
00:29:02,841 --> 00:29:05,844
I prepared two dishes
made with lots of buckwheat,

770
00:29:05,910 --> 00:29:07,946
which Yeo-jeong loves very much.

771
00:29:08,012 --> 00:29:09,447
First, buckwheat crêpe.

772
00:29:09,514 --> 00:29:11,082
-I see.
-Buckwheat crêpe.

773
00:29:11,149 --> 00:29:12,283
-Sounds great.
-It's usually

774
00:29:12,350 --> 00:29:15,854
filled with ripe kimchi and pork,
but I'll use seafood today.

775
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:17,288
-I see.
-That sounds good.

776
00:29:17,355 --> 00:29:19,390
Next, I'll use corn

777
00:29:19,457 --> 00:29:21,159
and make cold soup.

778
00:29:21,226 --> 00:29:23,094
-Sounds good.
-Cold soup?

779
00:29:23,161 --> 00:29:26,030
There's a French potato soup
called vichyssoise.

780
00:29:26,097 --> 00:29:27,799
Instead of potatoes,

781
00:29:27,866 --> 00:29:30,201
I'll use corn, chickpea, and oat milk.

782
00:29:30,268 --> 00:29:32,337
-Sounds good.
-I'll use those three

783
00:29:32,403 --> 00:29:34,239
-to make the cold soup.
-I see.

784
00:29:34,305 --> 00:29:35,807
You'll stop by Gangwon-do,

785
00:29:35,874 --> 00:29:37,242
then go to France.

786
00:29:39,911 --> 00:29:41,746
CHEF JONG-WON'S INGREDIENTS:
TOASTED BUCKWHEAT, MUNG BEAN

787
00:29:41,813 --> 00:29:43,982
RICE BREAD, COOKIE, PEACH, PLUM,
FIG, LEMON, OMIJA CHEONG, AND MORE

788
00:29:44,048 --> 00:29:47,218
Up against him is Chef Jong-won,
what are you making?

789
00:29:47,285 --> 00:29:49,454
When I saw you sitting there,

790
00:29:49,521 --> 00:29:54,159
you reminded me of a fairy,
or even an elf.

791
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:56,728
He's talking smooth again.

792
00:29:57,061 --> 00:29:59,130
THE ELOQUENCE THAT CAPTURED JUNG-HWAN

793
00:29:59,197 --> 00:30:01,366
-Nam-no has already lost.
-You do that a lot now.

794
00:30:01,432 --> 00:30:03,868
He called her fairy, <i>yojeong,</i>
not Yeo-jeong.

795
00:30:03,935 --> 00:30:06,538
-Like Tinkerbell.
-Tinkerbell.

796
00:30:06,604 --> 00:30:08,773
I want to accompany a fairy like you

797
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:11,409
as we take a journey for desserts.

798
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:12,644
-No way.
-Desserts.

799
00:30:12,710 --> 00:30:14,712
Here's the name of my dish.

800
00:30:14,779 --> 00:30:17,215
Born a Fairy, Yeo-jeong,

801
00:30:17,282 --> 00:30:19,918
Eat This Dessert and Pick Your J.

802
00:30:19,984 --> 00:30:22,387
I see.

803
00:30:22,453 --> 00:30:23,321
That's lengthy.

804
00:30:26,357 --> 00:30:27,592
It was too long.

805
00:30:27,659 --> 00:30:29,327
What's this dish like?

806
00:30:29,394 --> 00:30:31,963
-I prepared two dishes.
-Two dishes.

807
00:30:32,030 --> 00:30:33,398
-First, a tart.
-Tart.

808
00:30:33,464 --> 00:30:34,699
In the tart,

809
00:30:34,766 --> 00:30:36,901
I will add flan,
which is a type of custard.

810
00:30:36,968 --> 00:30:39,470
A flan for dessert.

811
00:30:39,537 --> 00:30:43,041
It's now summer,
so fresh fruit is in season.

812
00:30:43,107 --> 00:30:45,610
And these fruit aren't high in sugar,

813
00:30:45,677 --> 00:30:47,846
so you can enjoy them
without feeling guilty.

814
00:30:47,912 --> 00:30:50,515
Doesn't flan take a while to make?

815
00:30:50,582 --> 00:30:53,051
It does, but the method I'm using

816
00:30:53,117 --> 00:30:57,255
involves a microwave,
so it'll be quite easy to make.

817
00:30:57,322 --> 00:30:58,990
-There's a way?
-And next,

818
00:30:59,057 --> 00:31:00,959
I'll make a traditional beverage
called <i>omi-galsu</i>.

819
00:31:01,025 --> 00:31:03,595
It means "water that quenches thirst."

820
00:31:03,661 --> 00:31:05,830
It's made with either mung beans
or soybean juice.

821
00:31:05,897 --> 00:31:07,532
-Really?
-I'll use mung beans.

822
00:31:07,599 --> 00:31:08,933
Like <i>misugaru,</i> the grain drink.

823
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:12,003
So I'll use your <i>omija cheong</i>
and make two different items.

824
00:31:12,737 --> 00:31:15,740
-His focus is on dessert.
<i>-Misugaru.</i>

825
00:31:15,807 --> 00:31:19,244
All right, then. Let us begin this round.

826
00:31:19,811 --> 00:31:21,312
I'm nervous.

827
00:31:21,379 --> 00:31:23,781
"Cho Yeo-jeong has brought me up."

828
00:31:23,848 --> 00:31:27,852
Crushing on cooking, Chef Son Jong-won.

829
00:31:27,919 --> 00:31:31,222
But he says, "Please bring me up too."

830
00:31:31,289 --> 00:31:34,259
Crushing on stars, Chef Yoon Nam-no.

831
00:31:34,325 --> 00:31:37,195
Which one of them
will become Yeo-jeong's favorite?

832
00:31:37,262 --> 00:31:40,498
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

833
00:31:42,934 --> 00:31:44,402
Who'll become her bias?

834
00:31:44,469 --> 00:31:45,937
Begin!

835
00:31:46,004 --> 00:31:47,071
THE BIAS SHOWDOWN

836
00:31:47,639 --> 00:31:50,675
Who'll become her favorite, her bias?

837
00:31:50,742 --> 00:31:52,677
-Syrup?
-Jong-won or Nam-no?

838
00:31:52,744 --> 00:31:54,812
They have two distinct styles.

839
00:31:54,879 --> 00:31:57,849
If you fail to make flan once,
then you're done.

840
00:31:57,916 --> 00:31:59,751
-Really?
-There's no going back.

841
00:31:59,817 --> 00:32:01,619
-It takes a while too.
-I see.

842
00:32:01,686 --> 00:32:05,056
He'll have to use all 15 minutes,

843
00:32:05,123 --> 00:32:06,824
checking in every now and then.

844
00:32:06,891 --> 00:32:08,626
Flan isn't easy to make.

845
00:32:08,693 --> 00:32:12,063
-Chef Jong-won is flattening the bread.
-That's the rice bread.

846
00:32:12,130 --> 00:32:13,231
-The rice bread.
-Yes.

847
00:32:13,298 --> 00:32:15,600
It'll probably turn into a tart shell.

848
00:32:15,667 --> 00:32:18,202
He's making the tart shell
with rice bread?

849
00:32:18,269 --> 00:32:20,171
-Yes, you can often use bread.
-No way.

850
00:32:20,238 --> 00:32:23,107
Nam-no looks busy on the blender.

851
00:32:23,174 --> 00:32:25,877
-It's buckwheat.
-Buckwheat.

852
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:27,445
-It's the crêpe batter.
-For the crêpe.

853
00:32:27,512 --> 00:32:29,647
He's using buckwheat flour.

854
00:32:29,714 --> 00:32:32,317
-He's making the buckwheat crêpe.
-He's making the batter now?

855
00:32:32,383 --> 00:32:33,384
Done.

856
00:32:34,319 --> 00:32:35,153
OAT MILK

857
00:32:35,219 --> 00:32:36,321
CHICKPEA

858
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:38,122
The corn.

859
00:32:38,957 --> 00:32:41,626
Nam-no's using corn.

860
00:32:41,693 --> 00:32:43,261
Why do you have to taste so many things?

861
00:32:43,328 --> 00:32:44,929
He's blending that with corn.

862
00:32:45,530 --> 00:32:46,764
That's something else.

863
00:32:46,831 --> 00:32:48,533
The first one was for the crêpe.

864
00:32:48,599 --> 00:32:50,568
-The second is for the corn soup.
-The beverage.

865
00:32:50,635 --> 00:32:52,403
-He's adding ricotta.
-Ricotta.

866
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:55,139
-Ricotta?
-Because it's soup?

867
00:32:55,206 --> 00:32:58,676
He said it'd be like something
between porridge and soup.

868
00:32:59,043 --> 00:33:00,878
STRAINING THROUGH A SIEVE

869
00:33:00,945 --> 00:33:02,680
Nam-no looks dead serious.

870
00:33:02,747 --> 00:33:04,849
-He is.
-You should take Jong-won down.

871
00:33:04,916 --> 00:33:06,417
It's about time.

872
00:33:06,484 --> 00:33:08,219
-He'd better win today.
-Yes.

873
00:33:09,287 --> 00:33:11,022
THINLY PRESSED RICE BREAD

874
00:33:11,489 --> 00:33:13,524
REMOVING JUST THE CRUST

875
00:33:13,891 --> 00:33:14,792
CUT IN HALF!

876
00:33:16,928 --> 00:33:19,530
-He's putting them together.
-Huh?

877
00:33:19,597 --> 00:33:22,467
-It was small, so he's connecting them.
-He's sticking them together.

878
00:33:22,533 --> 00:33:24,635
Because the bread itself was too small?

879
00:33:24,702 --> 00:33:26,771
-The egg wash?
-What are you brushing on it?

880
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:28,439
-I'm buttering it.
-Butter.

881
00:33:28,506 --> 00:33:30,208
He puts butter on it and makes it bigger.

882
00:33:30,274 --> 00:33:31,709
To make it bigger?

883
00:33:31,776 --> 00:33:33,277
If you like it,

884
00:33:33,344 --> 00:33:34,679
I wanted you to take some home.

885
00:33:34,746 --> 00:33:36,047
HEHE

886
00:33:36,114 --> 00:33:37,815
-He'll pack some for you.
-And sit in her fridge.

887
00:33:37,882 --> 00:33:39,117
YAY

888
00:33:39,317 --> 00:33:40,485
CHUCKLE…

889
00:33:40,551 --> 00:33:44,122
He's now very good
at making his case with the guests.

890
00:33:44,188 --> 00:33:45,857
Nam-no, anything to-go?

891
00:33:45,923 --> 00:33:46,758
Nam-no.

892
00:33:46,824 --> 00:33:49,394
-No, he has to eat the rest.
-Nam-no.

893
00:33:49,460 --> 00:33:52,063
-Yes?
-He's offering something to-go.

894
00:33:52,130 --> 00:33:53,564
I'll make sure you take mine too.

895
00:33:53,631 --> 00:33:54,866
-It's okay.
-Will she have leftovers?

896
00:33:54,932 --> 00:33:56,634
I have a great feeling today.

897
00:33:56,701 --> 00:33:58,536
-He says he has a great feeling.
-Whoa.

898
00:33:58,603 --> 00:33:59,704
It must be good.

899
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,340
STILL MAKING THE TART SHELL

900
00:34:02,407 --> 00:34:04,142
He's spending a while on that.

901
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:06,411
He's putting it in a mold.

902
00:34:06,477 --> 00:34:09,313
-A pie mold.
-A pie mold.

903
00:34:09,380 --> 00:34:10,281
It's big.

904
00:34:10,815 --> 00:34:12,950
I didn't think he'd do it with rice bread.

905
00:34:13,017 --> 00:34:14,185
He's using bread to make that.

906
00:34:14,252 --> 00:34:15,086
How creative.

907
00:34:15,586 --> 00:34:16,654
BUT…

908
00:34:16,721 --> 00:34:18,222
Are you burning the syrup intentionally?

909
00:34:18,289 --> 00:34:19,424
It's burning.

910
00:34:19,490 --> 00:34:21,325
-What's burning?
-No.

911
00:34:21,392 --> 00:34:23,561
-Caramel.
-He's making caramel.

912
00:34:23,628 --> 00:34:25,129
Is that <i>dalgona?</i>

913
00:34:25,196 --> 00:34:26,497
-No?
-It's caramel.

914
00:34:26,564 --> 00:34:28,199
-Is that burnt?
-It's caramel.

915
00:34:28,266 --> 00:34:30,468
-It's too early to be happy.
-Wait.

916
00:34:30,535 --> 00:34:32,670
-It's burnt.
-It smells burnt.

917
00:34:32,737 --> 00:34:34,505
No, that's burnt.

918
00:34:34,572 --> 00:34:36,340
It's too early for him to be happy. No.

919
00:34:36,407 --> 00:34:38,276
It looks perfect.

920
00:34:38,342 --> 00:34:39,410
If it's brown, it's burnt.

921
00:34:39,477 --> 00:34:40,311
No, it's perfect.

922
00:34:40,378 --> 00:34:42,814
-He has to do it over.
-Sung-jun says it's perfect.

923
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:45,049
-He has to do it over.
-That's caramel?

924
00:34:45,116 --> 00:34:46,250
-Is that okay?
-It's caramel.

925
00:34:46,317 --> 00:34:48,019
What are those? What kind of beans?

926
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,220
They're like stones.

927
00:34:49,287 --> 00:34:53,224
-Pie weights.
-It makes sure the sheet doesn't rise.

928
00:34:53,291 --> 00:34:54,992
Without it, it can either rise or pop.

929
00:34:55,059 --> 00:34:56,928
Did you press start?

930
00:34:58,262 --> 00:34:59,597
Press start.

931
00:34:59,664 --> 00:35:01,065
I practically made that.

932
00:35:01,132 --> 00:35:02,600
-Chef Sung-jun…
-I saved it.

933
00:35:02,667 --> 00:35:04,702
…I'm rather grateful today.

934
00:35:04,769 --> 00:35:07,538
But rice bread,
as opposed to regular bread,

935
00:35:07,605 --> 00:35:09,474
is much denser and heavier,

936
00:35:09,540 --> 00:35:10,508
so it doesn't really rise.

937
00:35:11,209 --> 00:35:13,044
-I see. But don't let it rise.
-But still…

938
00:35:13,111 --> 00:35:14,312
How do you know these things?

939
00:35:14,378 --> 00:35:16,414
I just pick up things.

940
00:35:16,981 --> 00:35:18,616
It's nice to hear his comments here,

941
00:35:18,683 --> 00:35:19,517
but when you're out there,

942
00:35:19,584 --> 00:35:21,352
he's just a huge nuisance.

943
00:35:21,819 --> 00:35:23,521
A BITTER REMARK…

944
00:35:23,588 --> 00:35:26,224
And you're too busy to correct him
when he spreads false info.

945
00:35:26,290 --> 00:35:27,125
YOU'RE SO RIGHT

946
00:35:27,191 --> 00:35:29,227
Especially when he makes a scene
over a small mishap,

947
00:35:29,293 --> 00:35:31,062
as if I've committed a huge crime.

948
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:33,097
-It's burning!
-"It's really burnt!"

949
00:35:33,164 --> 00:35:35,600
Make one mistake, and I will point it out.

950
00:35:35,666 --> 00:35:37,101
Is that the crêpe?

951
00:35:38,336 --> 00:35:40,338
Make it thin, Nam-no.

952
00:35:40,404 --> 00:35:42,340
-That's nice.
-That's important.

953
00:35:42,406 --> 00:35:45,042
-He's making buckwheat crêpes.
-That's good.

954
00:35:45,109 --> 00:35:47,512
If you use only buckwheat,
it'll rip much more easily,

955
00:35:47,578 --> 00:35:51,115
so it looks like
he added some flour or starch.

956
00:35:51,182 --> 00:35:53,284
Make them thin. Nice job.

957
00:35:53,351 --> 00:35:55,319
Five minutes have gone by, ten left.

958
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:57,655
EGG

959
00:35:58,556 --> 00:35:59,390
ONE MORE

960
00:35:59,657 --> 00:36:03,728
3. BEAT EGGS, ADD OAT MILK AND SUGAR

961
00:36:03,794 --> 00:36:05,830
He's making the flan base.

962
00:36:05,897 --> 00:36:07,665
-That's flan?
-That's the flan base.

963
00:36:07,732 --> 00:36:09,934
Jong-won's making flan.

964
00:36:10,001 --> 00:36:11,068
Flan.

965
00:36:11,135 --> 00:36:11,969
BUTTER THE BOWL

966
00:36:12,436 --> 00:36:14,505
ABOUT TO ADD CARAMEL, BUT…

967
00:36:15,339 --> 00:36:16,174
-Argh.
-What?

968
00:36:16,240 --> 00:36:18,376
-It's an emergency.
-It hardened.

969
00:36:18,442 --> 00:36:20,378
-I told you so. It's ruined.
-It's solid.

970
00:36:20,444 --> 00:36:21,712
-What now?
-It's solid.

971
00:36:21,779 --> 00:36:23,481
-It's your time.
-That's ruined.

972
00:36:23,548 --> 00:36:27,051
He left it over iced water,
so the caramel hardened.

973
00:36:27,118 --> 00:36:28,686
It's made of sugar,

974
00:36:28,753 --> 00:36:30,321
so it becomes solid when cooled.

975
00:36:30,388 --> 00:36:31,856
Microwave.

976
00:36:31,923 --> 00:36:34,358
-I see.
-Here's what flan is.

977
00:36:34,425 --> 00:36:36,327
It's similar to pudding,

978
00:36:36,394 --> 00:36:39,330
and the caramel sauce on top
is supposed to drizzle down.

979
00:36:39,397 --> 00:36:40,865
But that became solid.

980
00:36:40,932 --> 00:36:41,832
Microwave.

981
00:36:42,967 --> 00:36:45,636
-Sometimes it goes over a tart, right?
-Yes.

982
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:47,572
-That's flan.
-It melted.

983
00:36:47,638 --> 00:36:49,774
-It did? Okay.
-Wow.

984
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:51,008
He quickly melted it.

985
00:36:51,075 --> 00:36:54,445
It'd better not mix with water.
