I do that when I drink hot soup.

1227
00:45:37,401 --> 00:45:41,839
I saw you working with my favorite <i>tteok.</i>

1228
00:45:41,905 --> 00:45:44,007
This used to be her breakfast.

1229
00:45:44,074 --> 00:45:45,576
HER BREAKFAST TTEOK'S MAKEOVER

1230
00:45:45,776 --> 00:45:47,010
-Whoa.
-Yes?

1231
00:45:47,945 --> 00:45:49,079
-We got a "whoa."
-Must be good.

1232
00:45:49,146 --> 00:45:50,948
-Hmm?
-They must go well.

1233
00:45:51,014 --> 00:45:53,117
Was there an unexpected twist?

1234
00:45:53,183 --> 00:45:55,986
Why does it taste zesty like fruit?
I just had <i>tteok.</i>

1235
00:45:56,053 --> 00:45:58,222
I added a dash of lemon zest.

1236
00:45:58,655 --> 00:46:01,658
LEMON ZEST FOR TANG
AND TRUFFLE SEASONING

1237
00:46:01,725 --> 00:46:03,327
You're like a magician.

1238
00:46:03,393 --> 00:46:06,230
She asked, "Why is this <i>tteok</i> zesty?"

1239
00:46:06,296 --> 00:46:07,731
She seems surprised.

1240
00:46:07,798 --> 00:46:09,800
But the corn flavor isn't too strong.

1241
00:46:09,867 --> 00:46:12,369
-So it's corn and…
-Chickpeas.

1242
00:46:12,436 --> 00:46:13,837
<i>-Chickpeas.</i>
<i>-Chickpeas.</i>

1243
00:46:13,904 --> 00:46:16,607
<i>-And then what?</i>
<i>-Oat milk.</i>

1244
00:46:16,673 --> 00:46:18,142
Chickpeas are so good for you.

1245
00:46:20,043 --> 00:46:21,411
-What's it like?
-It's so good.

1246
00:46:21,478 --> 00:46:23,247
-It's so good?
-Yes.

1247
00:46:23,313 --> 00:46:24,581
Does it taste nutty?

1248
00:46:24,648 --> 00:46:26,049
It does.

1249
00:46:26,116 --> 00:46:28,285
Yet it's so tangy,
thanks to the lemon zest.

1250
00:46:28,352 --> 00:46:30,087
-Hey.
-It's not too rich.

1251
00:46:30,154 --> 00:46:31,688
Great job with that.

1252
00:46:31,755 --> 00:46:33,590
Just by looking at it,

1253
00:46:33,657 --> 00:46:35,793
I expected it to only taste
clean and nutty.

1254
00:46:35,859 --> 00:46:37,728
<i>So that tang must've been a twist.</i>

1255
00:46:37,795 --> 00:46:39,963
<i>Yes, and the mugwort flavor.</i>

1256
00:46:40,030 --> 00:46:41,431
It's absolutely delicious.

1257
00:46:41,498 --> 00:46:42,933
I want a huge batch of it.

1258
00:46:43,000 --> 00:46:45,335
She wants a huge batch of it.

1259
00:46:45,402 --> 00:46:47,538
I'll make you this much.

1260
00:46:47,604 --> 00:46:49,640
Please pack some up to-go.

1261
00:46:49,706 --> 00:46:51,942
Next, the mung bean and buckwheat crêpe.

1262
00:46:52,009 --> 00:46:53,477
He considered your constitution

1263
00:46:53,544 --> 00:46:56,880
and made sure
the dish didn't go overboard.

1264
00:46:56,947 --> 00:47:00,717
Also, it's less greasy
than your usual buckwheat crêpes.

1265
00:47:00,784 --> 00:47:02,152
-It looks clean.
-It would be.

1266
00:47:02,219 --> 00:47:04,154
Should I eat it with chopsticks?

1267
00:47:04,221 --> 00:47:06,089
If you can, in one bite.

1268
00:47:06,156 --> 00:47:09,059
-In one bite?
-It might be difficult for her.

1269
00:47:09,126 --> 00:47:11,495
-Can she fit that into her mouth?
-I can.

1270
00:47:11,562 --> 00:47:13,463
-She'll give it a try.
-Is it too big?

1271
00:47:14,998 --> 00:47:16,667
TOTALLY POSSIBLE

1272
00:47:17,067 --> 00:47:18,368
She eats very well.

1273
00:47:20,003 --> 00:47:21,305
Mmm!

1274
00:47:22,372 --> 00:47:23,774
YES!

1275
00:47:23,841 --> 00:47:25,442
She sounds amazed.

1276
00:47:25,509 --> 00:47:28,111
AN APPLAUSE

1277
00:47:28,178 --> 00:47:29,746
-What?
-Do you like it?

1278
00:47:29,813 --> 00:47:32,382
-It's so good.
-Is it that good?

1279
00:47:32,449 --> 00:47:34,151
It's very clean.

1280
00:47:34,218 --> 00:47:36,086
I also love squid <i>sundae,</i>

1281
00:47:36,753 --> 00:47:39,957
and it reminds me of that too.

1282
00:47:40,023 --> 00:47:41,792
<i>You're right. I used squid.</i>

1283
00:47:41,859 --> 00:47:42,960
<i>She must like it.</i>

1284
00:47:43,026 --> 00:47:46,763
<i>On top of that, toasted buckwheat</i>
<i>adds such a nice texture.</i>

1285
00:47:46,830 --> 00:47:48,632
It's fantastic. I mean it.

1286
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:50,000
Thank you.

1287
00:47:50,067 --> 00:47:52,236
It's such a wonder
that you can still talk so well

1288
00:47:52,302 --> 00:47:53,537
with food in your mouth.

1289
00:47:54,571 --> 00:47:56,874
If it were us, it'd fly everywhere.

1290
00:47:56,940 --> 00:48:00,010
-And her pronunciation is right on.
-I was surprised.

1291
00:48:00,077 --> 00:48:02,579
-She clearly had food in her mouth.
-She was chewing.

1292
00:48:02,646 --> 00:48:04,414
Because I have to do lines
while eating sometimes.

1293
00:48:04,481 --> 00:48:06,116
SO SHE ENUNCIATES

1294
00:48:06,183 --> 00:48:07,885
-Yes.
-I knew it.

1295
00:48:07,951 --> 00:48:11,154
-That's what you do as an actor.
-Right? We could never do that.

1296
00:48:11,221 --> 00:48:13,724
I had to read my lines while eating
in the Chapaguri scene too.

1297
00:48:13,790 --> 00:48:15,425
Yes, you were eating.

1298
00:48:15,492 --> 00:48:16,860
-It's a wonder.
-I think I remember.

1299
00:48:16,927 --> 00:48:19,529
-If it were us, it'd fly out.
-Everywhere.

1300
00:48:19,596 --> 00:48:21,331
-It'd be a mess.
-We can't keep it in.

1301
00:48:21,398 --> 00:48:22,499
GLAD SHE'S EATING ALONE

1302
00:48:22,566 --> 00:48:26,103
-Nam-no actually stayed focused today.
-He did.

1303
00:48:26,169 --> 00:48:28,071
I caught you with my piggy data network.

1304
00:48:29,473 --> 00:48:30,340
-Piggy data.
-Wait.

1305
00:48:30,407 --> 00:48:34,878
-Will Nam-no finally win against Jong-won?
-It's so good.

1306
00:48:34,945 --> 00:48:37,481
He'll probably get lots of points.

1307
00:48:37,547 --> 00:48:40,684
-It was so good.
-Please try Jong-won's dish now.

1308
00:48:41,084 --> 00:48:45,155
FLAN TOPPED WITH SEASONAL FRUIT
FOR THE DESSERT FAIRY

1309
00:48:46,223 --> 00:48:49,893
OMI-GALSU TO BEAT THE HEAT
AND RECHARGE ENERGY

1310
00:48:51,161 --> 00:48:54,831
BORN A FAIRY, YEO-JEONG,
EAT THIS DESSERT AND PICK YOUR J

1311
00:48:54,898 --> 00:48:56,667
How should she eat this?

1312
00:48:56,733 --> 00:48:59,102
Mung beans help greatly with digestion.

1313
00:48:59,169 --> 00:49:02,472
-Have a sip of the beverage first.
-The beverage first.

1314
00:49:02,539 --> 00:49:05,075
-Isn't the color gorgeous?
<i>-Omi-galsu.</i>

1315
00:49:05,142 --> 00:49:06,677
The color suits her.

1316
00:49:06,743 --> 00:49:08,445
Yes, it fits her image.

1317
00:49:08,512 --> 00:49:09,680
-Whoa.
-Must be refreshing.

1318
00:49:09,746 --> 00:49:10,747
This is…

1319
00:49:10,814 --> 00:49:13,350
-This is so good.
-I see.

1320
00:49:13,417 --> 00:49:17,321
-It must make a nice starter.
-I knew it.

1321
00:49:17,387 --> 00:49:19,623
<i>Omija </i>means
that it has five different flavor notes,

1322
00:49:19,690 --> 00:49:21,258
and it's a great partner to mung beans.

1323
00:49:21,325 --> 00:49:23,460
I guess <i>omija </i>and mung beans go well.

1324
00:49:25,295 --> 00:49:27,864
I must've become thirsty
while watching them cook.

1325
00:49:29,566 --> 00:49:31,301
It must be good. She keeps going for it.

1326
00:49:31,368 --> 00:49:33,837
<i>Omija</i> and mung beans.
She's almost done with it.

1327
00:49:33,904 --> 00:49:35,605
That's <i>galsu.</i>

1328
00:49:35,672 --> 00:49:37,708
Mung beans don't taste dry.

1329
00:49:37,774 --> 00:49:40,277
I squeezed out just its juice.

1330
00:49:40,344 --> 00:49:43,013
<i>-I squeezed it out.</i>
<i>-Just the juice.</i>

1331
00:49:43,080 --> 00:49:44,715
<i>You did that in that short while?</i>

1332
00:49:44,781 --> 00:49:46,817
Did you add sparkling water?

1333
00:49:46,883 --> 00:49:48,552
<i>It's </i>omija cheong<i>, mung bean juice,</i>

1334
00:49:48,618 --> 00:49:50,587
<i>boiled, cooled,</i>

1335
00:49:50,654 --> 00:49:53,523
<i>then I added some sparkling water</i>
<i>since you seemed to like it.</i>

1336
00:49:53,590 --> 00:49:56,059
That's why it feels like champagne.

1337
00:49:56,126 --> 00:49:58,428
I can probably try to make this.

1338
00:49:58,495 --> 00:50:00,163
-That's nice.
-Because she doesn't drink.

1339
00:50:00,230 --> 00:50:03,266
-It's really good.
-She seems impressed.

1340
00:50:03,333 --> 00:50:04,534
How about this?

1341
00:50:04,601 --> 00:50:07,504
-Everything to the bottom.
-I should have everything, right?

1342
00:50:07,571 --> 00:50:11,908
-The pie.
-There was trouble with his flan,

1343
00:50:11,975 --> 00:50:13,744
but he covered it up with fruit.

1344
00:50:13,810 --> 00:50:15,879
It's the same once you eat it.

1345
00:50:15,946 --> 00:50:18,982
Thankfully, this was the first time
I had heard of flan,

1346
00:50:19,049 --> 00:50:20,984
-so it's fine.
-Is it?

1347
00:50:21,051 --> 00:50:23,553
-Is it like pudding?
-Yes, it's pretty much pudding.

1348
00:50:23,620 --> 00:50:25,555
-All right.
-She already looks happy.

1349
00:50:25,622 --> 00:50:28,792
Yes, she has a sweet tooth,
but she had been holding herself back.

1350
00:50:28,859 --> 00:50:30,594
WHAT'S IT LIKE?

1351
00:50:33,163 --> 00:50:34,965
MMM

1352
00:50:35,232 --> 00:50:36,366
CAN'T HIDE HER HAPPINESS

1353
00:50:36,433 --> 00:50:37,868
Buckwheat, emergency.

1354
00:50:37,934 --> 00:50:41,938
-I'm astonished at the dessert right away.
-Right? It comes to you so naturally.

1355
00:50:42,005 --> 00:50:43,173
You can taste that sweetness.

1356
00:50:43,240 --> 00:50:46,877
I don't know if this is right
because I haven't had flan before,

1357
00:50:46,943 --> 00:50:49,479
but with the rice bread you used,

1358
00:50:49,546 --> 00:50:53,950
it's like a really delicious French toast
I can have as a meal.

1359
00:50:54,017 --> 00:50:56,853
It tastes more like a meal.

1360
00:50:56,920 --> 00:50:57,954
It's so good.

1361
00:50:58,021 --> 00:51:01,058
I guess it's more than a dessert

1362
00:51:01,124 --> 00:51:03,393
-if she says it could be a meal.
-Yes.

1363
00:51:03,460 --> 00:51:06,730
She thinks she could have this as a meal.

1364
00:51:06,797 --> 00:51:07,864
Mmm.

1365
00:51:07,931 --> 00:51:12,169
We thought Nam-no would win easily,
but there was a bit of a twist.

1366
00:51:12,235 --> 00:51:13,670
What's this jam?

1367
00:51:13,737 --> 00:51:17,507
<i>Blueberry jam and whipped ricotta.</i>

1368
00:51:18,475 --> 00:51:19,743
He added some at the end.

1369
00:51:19,810 --> 00:51:22,379
He tried his best
with blueberry jam and ricotta.

1370
00:51:22,446 --> 00:51:24,548
It'd make a good breakfast, right?

1371
00:51:24,614 --> 00:51:26,583
I often make French toast,

1372
00:51:26,650 --> 00:51:30,754
along with blueberry jam
or actual berries,

1373
00:51:30,821 --> 00:51:31,988
as well as some ricotta.

1374
00:51:32,789 --> 00:51:34,891
This seems like
a luxurious version of that.

1375
00:51:36,726 --> 00:51:38,228
How am I supposed to choose?

1376
00:51:38,295 --> 00:51:39,930
-That's up to you.
-That's up to you.

1377
00:51:40,530 --> 00:51:42,332
-This is too cruel.
-That's the point.

1378
00:51:43,200 --> 00:51:45,535
You can continue to try them
before you decide.

1379
00:51:45,602 --> 00:51:47,871
-She should.
-They are too different.

1380
00:51:47,938 --> 00:51:50,140
Do you have some for Seok-jin?

1381
00:51:50,507 --> 00:51:51,541
CHEF NAM-NO'S DISH FIRST

1382
00:51:51,608 --> 00:51:52,742
No way.

1383
00:51:52,809 --> 00:51:54,945
Seok-jin may have a different taste.

1384
00:51:55,011 --> 00:51:56,880
-He said to sip this first.
-Sip it first.

1385
00:51:57,547 --> 00:51:59,182
Chef Nam-no's dishes.

1386
00:52:03,353 --> 00:52:04,488
-What's this face?
-He's pleased.

1387
00:52:04,554 --> 00:52:08,291
It smelled like fruit,

1388
00:52:08,992 --> 00:52:11,962
but it tastes like legumes in my mouth.

1389
00:52:13,430 --> 00:52:15,265
It must be a wonder to you.

1390
00:52:15,332 --> 00:52:16,600
NEXT, WITH THE MUGWORT TTEOK

1391
00:52:16,666 --> 00:52:17,701
Mugwort <i>tteok.</i>

1392
00:52:18,969 --> 00:52:21,171
He found a piece of <i>tteok </i>inside.

1393
00:52:21,238 --> 00:52:22,606
Isn't the <i>tteok </i>good?

1394
00:52:22,672 --> 00:52:23,807
Don't force anything.

1395
00:52:24,474 --> 00:52:26,143
Because I love mugwort <i>tteok.</i>

1396
00:52:26,209 --> 00:52:27,310
FORCING HIM

1397
00:52:27,377 --> 00:52:30,514
It could've been
a bit boring if it were just this soup,

1398
00:52:30,580 --> 00:52:32,549
but this <i>tteok</i>
adds a hearty side to the soup.

1399
00:52:32,616 --> 00:52:33,950
HEARTY

1400
00:52:34,017 --> 00:52:37,087
Did you notice a bit of France?
You should be there too.

1401
00:52:37,154 --> 00:52:38,822
I'm not so sure about the location.

1402
00:52:39,990 --> 00:52:42,325
-It's just good.
-It's good.

1403
00:52:42,392 --> 00:52:43,260
Also,

1404
00:52:43,326 --> 00:52:46,763
it reached a part of my brain
that has never experienced this flavor.

1405
00:52:46,963 --> 00:52:48,298
REVIEWING LIKE AN ENGINEERING MAJOR

1406
00:52:48,365 --> 00:52:50,167
The buckwheat crêpe.

1407
00:52:52,469 --> 00:52:54,671
SMILES BIG AS SOON AS HE EATS IT

1408
00:52:54,738 --> 00:52:56,540
It must be that good.

1409
00:52:56,606 --> 00:52:58,275
This feels so good.

1410
00:52:58,341 --> 00:52:59,843
I'm not sure about going to Paris,

1411
00:53:00,477 --> 00:53:01,811
but I did a layover in Bangkok.

1412
00:53:03,613 --> 00:53:06,449
AN EXPECTED LAYOVER

1413
00:53:06,516 --> 00:53:08,218
<i>-It's the celery.</i>
<i>-It must be the celery.</i>

1414
00:53:08,285 --> 00:53:11,221
There's this vague Southeast Asian feel.
It's seasoned to perfection.

1415
00:53:12,189 --> 00:53:14,558
When you imagine a healthy dish,

1416
00:53:14,624 --> 00:53:17,427
you think of something
that doesn't taste that good.

1417
00:53:17,494 --> 00:53:18,728
But that's not the case here at all.

1418
00:53:18,795 --> 00:53:20,130
That's the best, then.

1419
00:53:20,197 --> 00:53:23,266
If it's both delicious and healthy,
that's simply the best.

1420
00:53:23,333 --> 00:53:25,602
Next, Chef Jong-won's dishes.

1421
00:53:26,102 --> 00:53:29,439
-Try the <i>omi-galsu</i> first.
<i>-Omi-galsu.</i>

1422
00:53:29,506 --> 00:53:30,774
-It's a traditional beverage.
-Huh?

1423
00:53:30,840 --> 00:53:32,709
-Man.
-Isn't it good?

1424
00:53:33,310 --> 00:53:35,645
-There goes the old dude. "Man."
-The old dude?

1425
00:53:36,479 --> 00:53:38,548
-Whoa.
-Whoa.

1426
00:53:38,615 --> 00:53:41,451
He goes, "Man,"
while having some beverage.

1427
00:53:41,518 --> 00:53:43,553
He's one of us now.

1428
00:53:43,620 --> 00:53:47,224
It tastes like royal court cuisine.

1429
00:53:47,290 --> 00:53:50,193
<i>-It must taste traditional.</i>
<i>-The </i>omija<i>.</i>

1430
00:53:50,260 --> 00:53:51,394
It has that flavor.

1431
00:53:51,461 --> 00:53:52,562
And next.

1432
00:53:52,629 --> 00:53:53,863
She ate it like this, right?

1433
00:53:54,598 --> 00:53:55,699
Everything together.

1434
00:53:57,234 --> 00:53:58,768
He tried to make flan.

1435
00:53:59,803 --> 00:54:01,538
Does everything go well together?

1436
00:54:02,372 --> 00:54:03,540
Mmm.

1437
00:54:03,740 --> 00:54:04,874
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1438
00:54:04,941 --> 00:54:06,676
It tastes Gen Z.

1439
00:54:06,743 --> 00:54:09,112
-Like Gen Z?
-Gen Z?

1440
00:54:09,179 --> 00:54:11,481
Is that positive or negative?

1441
00:54:11,548 --> 00:54:15,485
It's something trendy restaurants
tend to sell.

1442
00:54:15,552 --> 00:54:16,987
-Right.
-I see.

1443
00:54:17,053 --> 00:54:18,955
-Like a place in Seongsu-dong.
-A hip area.

1444
00:54:19,522 --> 00:54:20,590
Sexy food.

1445
00:54:21,258 --> 00:54:22,959
-Sexy food?
-This is bad.

1446
00:54:23,026 --> 00:54:25,362
It's like a place
popular with influencers,

1447
00:54:25,428 --> 00:54:28,732
so I took a bite without expecting much,

1448
00:54:28,798 --> 00:54:31,668
but I'm left thinking, "Well, it is good."

1449
00:54:32,302 --> 00:54:35,071
He's much better at commenting.
This is sad for me.

1450
00:54:35,405 --> 00:54:37,374
FEELING BAD

1451
00:54:37,440 --> 00:54:40,176
-I should've talked like him.
-It's all right.

1452
00:54:40,243 --> 00:54:41,978
And now, please make a decision.

1453
00:54:42,045 --> 00:54:44,514
-Oh, gosh.
-It's a difficult decision to make.

1454
00:54:44,581 --> 00:54:46,850
<i>Press one for Son Jong-won</i>

1455
00:54:46,916 --> 00:54:49,119
<i>and two for Nam-no.</i>

1456
00:54:49,185 --> 00:54:50,754
Make your decision

1457
00:54:50,820 --> 00:54:52,289
and press the button!

1458
00:54:52,355 --> 00:54:53,556
PUSH

1459
00:54:54,124 --> 00:54:56,426
-I did.
-You did?

1460
00:54:56,493 --> 00:54:57,827
You said it was too cruel.

1461
00:54:57,894 --> 00:55:00,230
-It is.
-You said it was difficult.

1462
00:55:00,297 --> 00:55:02,098
-But she chose quickly.
-That was quick.

1463
00:55:02,165 --> 00:55:04,601
Which one did Yeo-jeong choose?

1464
00:55:04,668 --> 00:55:06,369
Let's find out!

1465
00:55:07,804 --> 00:55:10,674
Jong-won currently has ten stars.

1466
00:55:10,740 --> 00:55:12,342
Nam-no has two.

1467
00:55:12,409 --> 00:55:14,944
And Jong-won has never lost to Nam-no.

1468
00:55:15,011 --> 00:55:16,646
A constitution-friendly journey!

1469
00:55:16,713 --> 00:55:18,181
Who did you choose?

1470
00:55:18,248 --> 00:55:21,484
Who helped Yeo-jeong
with her constitution-friendly diet?

1471
00:55:22,152 --> 00:55:25,221
Who helped Yeo-jeong
with her constitution-friendly diet?

1472
00:55:25,889 --> 00:55:26,723
Who is it?

1473
00:55:26,790 --> 00:55:27,657
SON JONG-WON WINS

1474
00:55:27,724 --> 00:55:29,025
JONG-WON WINS

1475
00:55:29,092 --> 00:55:31,227
-Jong-won wins.
-I can't believe it.

1476
00:55:31,294 --> 00:55:32,696
Son Jong-won.

1477
00:55:32,762 --> 00:55:34,597
He's strong against Nam-no.

1478
00:55:34,664 --> 00:55:36,766
WON ALL 5 ROUNDS AGAINST NAM-NO

1479
00:55:36,833 --> 00:55:38,468
Everything was good,

1480
00:55:38,535 --> 00:55:41,805
but it was the fact that
Chef Jong-won decided to make dessert.

1481
00:55:41,871 --> 00:55:43,406
That was a huge plus for me.

1482
00:55:43,473 --> 00:55:46,910
I love desserts so much,
but I usually have to hold back.

1483
00:55:46,976 --> 00:55:50,013
<i>But if I eat this as a meal,</i>
<i>I'd be satisfied after this.</i>

1484
00:55:50,080 --> 00:55:52,282
<i>It'd be a meal for me, and it was so good.</i>

1485
00:55:52,349 --> 00:55:54,918
Nam-no's dish
calls for that dessert after.

1486
00:55:54,984 --> 00:55:57,520
-You can eat more after.
-I wanted dessert.

1487
00:55:57,587 --> 00:55:59,289
-She can't stay in shape, then.
-It was good.

1488
00:55:59,356 --> 00:56:02,659
This means her bias is Jong-won now.

1489
00:56:02,726 --> 00:56:04,761
Let's hear it from him.

1490
00:56:04,828 --> 00:56:08,998
It was such an honor
for me to cook for an actor

1491
00:56:09,065 --> 00:56:10,567
who gave me such a big comfort.

1492
00:56:11,201 --> 00:56:13,336
Thank you for enjoying the dish.

1493
00:56:15,638 --> 00:56:17,540
Please put a star on him.

1494
00:56:17,607 --> 00:56:19,743
-This is his 11th win.
-Whoa.

1495
00:56:19,809 --> 00:56:21,911
The sole 1st place with 11 wins.

1496
00:56:21,978 --> 00:56:23,012
WIDENING THE GAP

1497
00:56:23,079 --> 00:56:24,614
Yeo-jeong chose you.

1498
00:56:24,681 --> 00:56:26,316
Congratulations.

1499
00:56:26,850 --> 00:56:30,320
-Let's take ten.
-Let's take ten minutes off.

1500
00:56:30,387 --> 00:56:31,588
Should I just eat this?

1501
00:56:31,654 --> 00:56:32,822
It was so good.

1502
00:56:32,889 --> 00:56:34,057
GIVING UP THE BREAK

1503
00:56:34,691 --> 00:56:36,059
Oh, then…

1504
00:56:36,126 --> 00:56:37,627
Min-hyeong!

1505
00:56:37,694 --> 00:56:38,528
CALLS SOMEONE OVER

1506
00:56:38,595 --> 00:56:41,965
YEO-JEONG'S MANAGER

1507
00:56:42,198 --> 00:56:43,166
SHARES WITH THE MANAGER

1508
00:56:43,233 --> 00:56:44,434
It's so good.

1509
00:56:46,436 --> 00:56:49,205
Doesn't it remind you of squid <i>sundae?</i>

1510
00:56:49,839 --> 00:56:51,541
And have a sip of this.

1511
00:56:52,242 --> 00:56:54,010
-Are you done with this?
-Yes.

1512
00:56:54,077 --> 00:56:55,278
It's really good.

1513
00:56:55,345 --> 00:56:56,379
CHUGS

1514
00:56:56,446 --> 00:56:58,047
Why are you drinking that?

1515
00:56:58,114 --> 00:56:59,582
That was really good.

1516
00:57:00,150 --> 00:57:02,919
AS ALWAYS, FINISHED THE LEFTOVERS

1517
00:57:02,986 --> 00:57:07,023
<i>Let us begin the second cook-off</i>
<i>with Yeo-jeong's ingredients.</i>

1518
00:57:07,090 --> 00:57:09,192
The leading authority
of cheat day meals on the show,

1519
00:57:09,259 --> 00:57:11,227
-Webtoon Artist Kim Poong.
-"Leading authority"?

1520
00:57:11,294 --> 00:57:14,998
He's up against Chef Jung Ho-young,
whose every day is a cheat day.

1521
00:57:15,064 --> 00:57:19,335
Poong poses a huge problem to Ho-young.

1522
00:57:19,402 --> 00:57:23,006
You've only lost against him recently,
putting you at four straight losses.

1523
00:57:23,072 --> 00:57:24,307
-Really?
-Really?

1524
00:57:24,707 --> 00:57:25,975
OUT OF HIS ELEMENT WHEN FACING POONG

1525
00:57:26,042 --> 00:57:28,111
-Did you think he'd be too easy?
-How shocking.

1526
00:57:28,178 --> 00:57:31,347
I ran into him a few days ago
outside the studio,

1527
00:57:31,414 --> 00:57:33,817
and he was such an eyesore
for some reason.

1528
00:57:34,484 --> 00:57:36,853
But I didn't know why,
so I thought about it.

1529
00:57:36,920 --> 00:57:38,121
Understandable.

1530
00:57:38,188 --> 00:57:40,190
It's partially for my recent losses,

1531
00:57:40,256 --> 00:57:42,892
and partially because of his smugness.

1532
00:57:43,693 --> 00:57:45,562
SMUG ABOUT HIS STARS

1533
00:57:45,628 --> 00:57:47,297
We received a transcript.

1534
00:57:47,363 --> 00:57:49,799
He'll be a bigger eyesore after this.

1535
00:57:49,866 --> 00:57:51,334
"To me,

1536
00:57:51,401 --> 00:57:55,071
Ho-young's level of Poongphobia
is as high as Nam-no's."

1537
00:57:55,972 --> 00:57:59,008
So Ho-young and Nam-no
are the same to you?

1538
00:57:59,075 --> 00:58:01,978
He's a star opener for me.

1539
00:58:02,045 --> 00:58:04,447
-A star opener?
-Like a bottle opener.

1540
00:58:04,514 --> 00:58:06,516
-Oh, my.
-A star opener.

1541
00:58:06,583 --> 00:58:09,385
-Aka an easy win.
-Yes.

1542
00:58:09,452 --> 00:58:10,687
I can tell by his face

1543
00:58:10,753 --> 00:58:12,188
that he feels winning is a given.

1544
00:58:12,255 --> 00:58:15,792
It's now about how big a win
he gets against him.

1545
00:58:15,859 --> 00:58:16,926
An overwhelming win.

1546
00:58:16,993 --> 00:58:18,394
A dramatic win.

1547
00:58:18,461 --> 00:58:19,496
A buzzworthy win.

1548
00:58:19,562 --> 00:58:21,464
-It's all about the buzzworthiness.
-Yes.

1549
00:58:21,531 --> 00:58:23,366
Ho-young will lose today.

1550
00:58:23,433 --> 00:58:24,567
FULL OF ANXIETY

1551
00:58:24,634 --> 00:58:26,970
-You seem rather grim.
-Make your case too.

1552
00:58:27,036 --> 00:58:29,873
If it were the old days,
I would've stepped in and said something,

1553
00:58:29,939 --> 00:58:32,876
but after consecutive losses,
I think I can understand Nam-no.

1554
00:58:32,942 --> 00:58:35,545
-I've been feeling small lately.
-Don't be.

1555
00:58:35,612 --> 00:58:36,946
Actually, my relationship

1556
00:58:37,013 --> 00:58:40,016
with my wife isn't so great
after my consecutive losses.

1557
00:58:40,083 --> 00:58:42,151
-You're bringing your family into this?
-His family.

1558
00:58:42,585 --> 00:58:45,788
FAMILY DISPUTE(?) DUE TO HIS LOSSES

1559
00:58:45,855 --> 00:58:49,526
Our biggest fights break out
whenever I lose to Poong.

1560
00:58:49,592 --> 00:58:51,394
She's like, "Aren't you ashamed?"

1561
00:58:51,461 --> 00:58:53,029
I'm rather worried right now.

1562
00:58:53,096 --> 00:58:54,497
THE PEACE IN HIS FAMILY IS AT STAKE

1563
00:58:55,365 --> 00:58:59,502
WEBTOON ARTIST POONG'S INGREDIENTS:
CUCUMBER, LEMON, HONEY, RICOTTA

1564
00:58:59,569 --> 00:59:01,738
What are you making today, Poong?

1565
00:59:01,804 --> 00:59:03,439
The name of my dish is

1566
00:59:04,040 --> 00:59:06,709
Pizza Nation, Princess Yeo-jeong.

1567
00:59:07,777 --> 00:59:09,946
-Pizza?
-Pizza Nation, Princess Yeo-jeong.

1568
00:59:10,013 --> 00:59:11,281
Oh, gosh.

1569
00:59:11,347 --> 00:59:13,249
-She said she loves pizza.
-This is cheating.

1570
00:59:13,316 --> 00:59:14,217
-So, pizza?
-Emergency.

1571
00:59:14,284 --> 00:59:16,252
The only time I make pizza

1572
00:59:16,753 --> 00:59:19,989
is when our guest is someone
who brought glory to our nation.

1573
00:59:20,056 --> 00:59:22,091
-I always made pizza.
-I'll leave this out here.

1574
00:59:22,158 --> 00:59:23,593
-He only makes it then.
-Yes.

1575
00:59:24,093 --> 00:59:26,195
HIS BEGINNING IS ALWAYS HUMBLE

1576
00:59:27,997 --> 00:59:29,532
BUT HIS WORKS ALWAYS END SUCCESSFULLY

1577
00:59:29,599 --> 00:59:32,769
-Those who brought glory to us.
-Those who did that.

1578
00:59:32,835 --> 00:59:36,139
-She did that through <i>Parasite</i>…
-And she did just that.

1579
00:59:36,205 --> 00:59:39,042
-…so it was about time I made pizza.
-So she's on that level.

1580
00:59:39,108 --> 00:59:42,211
On top of that, she said she likes pizza.

1581
00:59:42,278 --> 00:59:43,913
What I'm making today

1582
00:59:44,514 --> 00:59:46,015
is a cucumber pizza.

1583
00:59:46,082 --> 00:59:48,785
-Cucumber pizza?
-Cucumber?

1584
00:59:48,851 --> 00:59:50,086
Will it be okay?

1585
00:59:50,153 --> 00:59:52,422
I'll use cucumbers to--

1586
00:59:52,488 --> 00:59:54,090
-Turn it off.
-It's already an emergency.

1587
00:59:54,157 --> 00:59:56,793
-It's already an emergency.
-Hear me out first.

1588
00:59:56,859 --> 00:59:58,995
First, I'll make cucumber cream.

1589
00:59:59,062 --> 01:00:01,764
-Cucumber cream?
-Cucumber cream? Even worse.

1590
01:00:01,831 --> 01:00:05,501
These days, there are baguettes
filled with salted cucumber,

1591
01:00:05,568 --> 01:00:07,670
-like a sandwich.
-Something like that.

1592
01:00:07,737 --> 01:00:09,172
-It's the trend.
-Yes, you might've seen that,

1593
01:00:09,238 --> 01:00:12,108
but I am literally
turning cucumber into cream.

1594
01:00:12,175 --> 01:00:13,476
NEVER-BEFORE-SEEN CUCUMBER CREAM!

1595
01:00:13,543 --> 01:00:15,712
-So you won't see cucumber shapes?
-There will be a few.

1596
01:00:15,778 --> 01:00:17,647
I'm topping it with a layer of pickles.

1597
01:00:18,014 --> 01:00:18,848
ARGH

1598
01:00:18,915 --> 01:00:21,384
Also, the pizza dough will be deep-fried.

1599
01:00:21,451 --> 01:00:22,518
-Deep-fried?
-Deep-fried pizza?

1600
01:00:23,086 --> 01:00:24,687
RIGHT…

1601
01:00:24,754 --> 01:00:27,190
You're only thinking of online buzz.

1602
01:00:27,256 --> 01:00:28,958
No, it'll be good.

1603
01:00:29,025 --> 01:00:31,461
-Seok-jin isn't convinced either.
-Not by those words.

1604
01:00:31,527 --> 01:00:33,763
It's hard to imagine.

1605
01:00:33,830 --> 01:00:35,798
Many people are shaking their heads.

1606
01:00:35,865 --> 01:00:37,600
Is Poong going too far?

1607
01:00:37,667 --> 01:00:39,302
-No.
-A cucumber pizza.

1608
01:00:40,169 --> 01:00:42,338
CHEF HO-YOUNG'S INGREDIENTS:
OCTOPUS, SQUID, SHRIMP, POLLACK ROE

1609
01:00:42,405 --> 01:00:44,307
MOZZARELLA, CUCUMBER,
TOASTED BUCKWHEAT, LEMON, CILANTRO

1610
01:00:44,374 --> 01:00:47,477
Chef Ho-young, you're up against him,
so what are you making?

1611
01:00:47,543 --> 01:00:49,479
The dish I'm making

1612
01:00:49,545 --> 01:00:52,048
is for Yeo-jeong, the pretty girl.

1613
01:00:52,115 --> 01:00:53,716
I'm making stir-fried udon

1614
01:00:53,783 --> 01:00:55,685
with freshly pulled udon noodles.

1615
01:00:55,752 --> 01:00:57,920
-Fresh udon noodles?
-I saw seafood in your fridge,

1616
01:00:57,987 --> 01:00:59,889
so I'll use shrimp and squid,

1617
01:00:59,956 --> 01:01:02,125
then top it with pollack roe.

1618
01:01:02,191 --> 01:01:04,193
-He won already.
-I saw that

1619
01:01:04,260 --> 01:01:07,630
-she had octopus, so I'll make it tender…
-Octopus.

1620
01:01:07,697 --> 01:01:11,100
…and mix it with vinegar,
soy sauce, and lemon juice…

1621
01:01:11,167 --> 01:01:13,002
-That's his winning recipe.
-…for you to enjoy

1622
01:01:13,069 --> 01:01:16,439
tangy and creamy flavors at the same time.

1623
01:01:16,506 --> 01:01:18,574
Both dishes sound

1624
01:01:18,641 --> 01:01:19,709
equally delicious.

1625
01:01:19,776 --> 01:01:23,446
Pizza has always been my favorite,
so I even called it cheating,

1626
01:01:23,513 --> 01:01:26,983
but udon is also something
that I hold back from eating.

1627
01:01:27,984 --> 01:01:30,453
The udon already sounds so good.

1628
01:01:30,520 --> 01:01:32,588
It's been long since I've had it.

1629
01:01:32,655 --> 01:01:34,190
Do you want to decide first?

1630
01:01:34,424 --> 01:01:35,892
ALREADY DECIDED TO GO WITH UDON(?)

1631
01:01:35,958 --> 01:01:36,959
URGENT

1632
01:01:37,026 --> 01:01:39,095
-Mine is a dessert pizza.
-A dessert pizza.

1633
01:01:39,162 --> 01:01:41,497
-I see. A dessert pizza.
-A dessert pizza.

1634
01:01:41,564 --> 01:01:44,000
Because you thought she prefers desserts.

1635
01:01:44,067 --> 01:01:46,436
-So you jumped on it.
-I'm not always like that.

1636
01:01:46,502 --> 01:01:50,606
-I saw you doing that just now.
-She seems to vote for the dessert.

1637
01:01:50,673 --> 01:01:52,875
Come to think of it,
I'm serving the octopus as dessert.

1638
01:01:52,942 --> 01:01:54,377
-Octopus?
-Octopus dessert?

1639
01:01:54,444 --> 01:01:56,312
-Really?
-Octopus dessert?

1640
01:01:56,379 --> 01:01:57,914
JUST HAVING FUN

1641
01:01:57,980 --> 01:01:59,549
-What?
-And now,

1642
01:01:59,615 --> 01:02:03,553
let us begin this round,
Self-Discipline Was Just the Beginning.

1643
01:02:03,619 --> 01:02:06,389
Following Nam-no,
this man is ready to infect

1644
01:02:06,456 --> 01:02:10,159
Chef Ho-young with Poongphobia,
Webtoon Artist Kim Poong.

1645
01:02:10,827 --> 01:02:14,230
But this guy is here,
ready to make Yeo-jeong

1646
01:02:14,297 --> 01:02:16,999
look more like himself,
Chef Jung Ho-young.

1647
01:02:17,066 --> 01:02:19,736
Who's going to give Yeo-jeong
an irresistible appetite?

1648
01:02:19,802 --> 01:02:23,372
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

1649
01:02:24,607 --> 01:02:25,875
Begin!

1650
01:02:25,942 --> 01:02:27,677
LIVE FEED ON!

1651
01:02:28,444 --> 01:02:30,713
-Cooking wine.
-Self-discipline is off the table now.

1652
01:02:30,780 --> 01:02:33,483
-Yes. Octopus.
-She's looking to eat good.

1653
01:02:33,549 --> 01:02:35,785
Octopus becomes softer with cooking wine.

1654
01:02:36,085 --> 01:02:37,587
NEXT, SAUCE FOR THE STIR-FRIED UDON

1655
01:02:37,653 --> 01:02:41,157
Adding cooking wine
is a tip to make your octopus tender.

1656
01:02:41,424 --> 01:02:42,358
FLOUR, STARCH

1657
01:02:42,425 --> 01:02:44,260
And is he making dough?

1658
01:02:44,327 --> 01:02:45,428
For udon noodles.

1659
01:02:45,495 --> 01:02:46,996
He's making fresh noodles.

1660
01:02:48,498 --> 01:02:49,665
Fresh noodles.

1661
01:02:49,732 --> 01:02:52,235
-Huh? Emergency.
-It's an emergency.

1662
01:02:52,301 --> 01:02:53,336
-Why?
-Emergency.

1663
01:02:53,402 --> 01:02:56,305
-It's way too thin.
-It's too thin.

1664
01:02:56,372 --> 01:02:57,540
He needs more flour.

1665
01:02:57,607 --> 01:02:58,841
Or switch to <i>sujebi.</i>

1666
01:02:58,908 --> 01:03:00,610
<i>-Sujebi?</i>
-The batter was too watery.

1667
01:03:01,344 --> 01:03:02,812
He must be making fresh noodles.

1668
01:03:03,312 --> 01:03:04,781
He's peeling the cucumber.

1669
01:03:04,847 --> 01:03:06,282
He's peeling it to make cream.

1670
01:03:07,450 --> 01:03:10,353
But the peel has a better color
and a more vibrant smell.

1671
01:03:10,419 --> 01:03:13,823
The peel has a stronger smell

1672
01:03:13,890 --> 01:03:15,825
It'll smell grassy.

1673
01:03:15,892 --> 01:03:17,760
Have you made cucumber cream before?

1674
01:03:17,827 --> 01:03:21,030
Something similar,
but it's my first time with actual cream.

1675
01:03:21,097 --> 01:03:23,499
Yeo-jeong is slowly becoming suspicious.

1676
01:03:23,566 --> 01:03:26,002
"Are you sure you've made this before?"

1677
01:03:26,068 --> 01:03:27,303
I was just curious.

1678
01:03:27,370 --> 01:03:29,305
"If it's your first time,
you might ruin it."

1679
01:03:29,372 --> 01:03:31,307
So cucumber
is the main ingredient for him.

1680
01:03:31,374 --> 01:03:33,643
It's also in season in summer.

1681
01:03:33,709 --> 01:03:37,146
So I hope many people
watch this and try it at home.

1682
01:03:37,213 --> 01:03:39,015
-Butter in water?
-What's he doing?

1683
01:03:39,081 --> 01:03:40,817
-In the water?
-The water?

1684
01:03:40,883 --> 01:03:42,552
-Is that water or alcohol?
-Water.

1685
01:03:42,618 --> 01:03:43,920
Butter in water?

1686
01:03:43,986 --> 01:03:45,421
That's a French technique.

1687
01:03:45,488 --> 01:03:48,391
-I think he's making the dough.
-You're right.

1688
01:03:48,457 --> 01:03:49,992
-The pizza dough.
-Pizza dough.

1689
01:03:50,459 --> 01:03:52,728
UDON JUNG MAKES UDON NOODLES

1690
01:03:53,362 --> 01:03:55,832
Ho-young makes
fresh udon noodles from scratch.

1691
01:03:55,898 --> 01:03:58,534
The dough is still a bit too watery.

1692
01:03:59,202 --> 01:04:00,970
It's too watery, right?

1693
01:04:01,037 --> 01:04:03,105
That happens with dough
when the first try goes wrong.

1694
01:04:03,840 --> 01:04:05,842
-Hey.
-Hey.

1695
01:04:05,908 --> 01:04:07,577
-Emergency.
-It's falling apart.

1696
01:04:07,643 --> 01:04:08,978
THE EMERGENCY LIGHT IS BUSY TODAY

1697
01:04:09,045 --> 01:04:11,547
-It's an emergency.
-Ho-young, you have to do this.

1698
01:04:11,614 --> 01:04:12,782
UDON JUNG CAN'T SEEM TO SAVE HIS FACE…

1699
01:04:13,516 --> 01:04:15,484
-Switch it.
-Switch it to <i>sujebi.</i>

1700
01:04:15,551 --> 01:04:16,886
You should use your hands.

1701
01:04:16,953 --> 01:04:19,522
-My hands and feet are cold again.
-Right?

1702
01:04:19,589 --> 01:04:20,823
My gosh.

1703
01:04:21,891 --> 01:04:23,693
FOR NOW, LET IT REST!

1704
01:04:23,759 --> 01:04:26,629
-He's dropping it in there?
-He's adding flour to the pan.

1705
01:04:26,696 --> 01:04:28,331
-It's frying powder.
-Frying powder?

1706
01:04:28,397 --> 01:04:30,132
Poong's using frying powder?

1707
01:04:30,199 --> 01:04:32,702
-Is that for the dough?
-Yes, it's the dough.

1708
01:04:32,768 --> 01:04:34,937
That's the pizza dough.

1709
01:04:35,004 --> 01:04:36,672
-He just dropped an egg.
-An egg?

1710
01:04:36,739 --> 01:04:38,441
It's like choux dough, pate a choux.

1711
01:04:38,507 --> 01:04:40,343
-He's making pate a choux?
-It's pate a choux.

1712
01:04:40,409 --> 01:04:41,777
-It must be hot.
-Iron Palm training.

1713
01:04:41,844 --> 01:04:42,712
Isn't it hot?

1714
01:04:42,778 --> 01:04:44,780
I can do this for Princess Yeo-jeong.

1715
01:04:44,847 --> 01:04:46,048
For Princess Yeo-jeong…

1716
01:04:46,115 --> 01:04:47,316
It's hot!

1717
01:04:47,383 --> 01:04:48,885
It must be so hot.

1718
01:04:48,951 --> 01:04:51,087
-It's too hot.
-Use a blender.

1719
01:04:51,153 --> 01:04:52,855
-Careful.
-That'll turn into scrambled eggs.

1720
01:04:52,922 --> 01:04:54,223
Is it okay for the egg to cook?

1721
01:04:54,290 --> 01:04:55,858
-It's fine.
-Is it?

1722
01:04:55,925 --> 01:04:58,427
-It's okay.
-That's the pizza dough.

1723
01:04:58,494 --> 01:04:59,528
Right?

1724
01:04:59,595 --> 01:05:01,564
It'll rise when it's deep-fried…

1725
01:05:01,631 --> 01:05:04,600
-It rises?
-…without resting, unlike regular dough.

1726
01:05:04,667 --> 01:05:07,203
Otherwise, it'll be too hard,
so that's the only way.

1727
01:05:07,270 --> 01:05:11,440
-It's a unique way of making dough.
-It looks like a potato.

1728
01:05:11,507 --> 01:05:12,808
Can you mix this?

1729
01:05:13,075 --> 01:05:14,477
NO IS ON THE MOVE

1730
01:05:14,777 --> 01:05:17,580
4. MAKE OCTOPUS SAUCE
BY MIXING SUGAR, SOY SAUCE, AND VINEGAR

1731
01:05:17,847 --> 01:05:18,814
LINGERING LOOK

1732
01:05:18,881 --> 01:05:20,616
NO STIRS

1733
01:05:20,683 --> 01:05:22,551
Ho-young preps seafood.

1734
01:05:22,618 --> 01:05:23,953
Seafood. Shrimp and squid.

1735
01:05:25,087 --> 01:05:27,990
-I hope the noodles come out well.
-A retry.

1736
01:05:28,057 --> 01:05:31,260
-If it's too thin, it won't be good.
-It seems firmer.

1737
01:05:31,327 --> 01:05:35,097
-That's not it.
-I hope it works.

1738
01:05:35,164 --> 01:05:37,199
-Use your hands.
-It doesn't work!

1739
01:05:37,934 --> 01:05:40,069
You have ten minutes left.

1740
01:05:40,136 --> 01:05:43,472
It's taking Ho-young
more than five minutes to make dough.

1741
01:05:44,040 --> 01:05:45,274
Does he have to redo it?

1742
01:05:45,341 --> 01:05:46,309
THROW!

1743
01:05:46,375 --> 01:05:48,210
Ho-young looks mad.

1744
01:05:48,277 --> 01:05:50,079
LAUGHING

1745
01:05:50,146 --> 01:05:51,280
Things aren't going his way.

1746
01:05:51,347 --> 01:05:53,382
Good luck, Ho-young.

1747
01:05:53,449 --> 01:05:54,817
Keep folding the dough.

1748
01:05:54,884 --> 01:05:56,986
You can just make me <i>sujebi.</i>

1749
01:05:57,053 --> 01:06:00,222
Yeo-jeong couldn't take it
and said she was fine with <i>sujebi.</i>

1750
01:06:00,289 --> 01:06:01,490
I'm really fine.

1751
01:06:01,557 --> 01:06:02,858
Do you want some of mine?

1752
01:06:03,526 --> 01:06:04,427
Yes, give him yours.

1753
01:06:04,493 --> 01:06:07,897
But he wanted to make
udon noodles from scratch.

1754
01:06:07,964 --> 01:06:09,332
PRE-MADE SUJEBI

1755
01:06:09,398 --> 01:06:10,266
It's working.

1756
01:06:10,333 --> 01:06:12,335
It's happening!

1757
01:06:12,401 --> 01:06:13,235
RATTLE

1758
01:06:13,736 --> 01:06:16,238
IT FEELS A LITTLE LESS WATERY

1759
01:06:16,772 --> 01:06:17,807
RATTLE

1760
01:06:17,873 --> 01:06:19,642
I should hold the board for him.

1761
01:06:20,676 --> 01:06:22,545
-Let me hold it.
-Why won't it…

1762
01:06:23,646 --> 01:06:24,847
Jong-won steps in and helps.

1763
01:06:24,914 --> 01:06:26,449
He's an honorary firefighter.

1764
01:06:26,515 --> 01:06:28,818
It's nice that Jong-won is helping,

1765
01:06:28,884 --> 01:06:30,586
but his head is blocking the view

1766
01:06:30,653 --> 01:06:32,355
of the noodles coming out.

1767
01:06:36,492 --> 01:06:38,060
Jong-won, you have a pretty big head.

1768
01:06:38,728 --> 01:06:41,030
THE BIG-HEAD CHEF

1769
01:06:41,097 --> 01:06:42,631
We didn't see the noodles in the making.

1770
01:06:42,698 --> 01:06:45,701
-The noodles are ready.
-Or your body is too thin.

1771
01:06:45,768 --> 01:06:47,603
The udon noodles are ready.

1772
01:06:47,670 --> 01:06:50,072
We didn't see them being made
because of Jong-won's head.

1773
01:06:50,139 --> 01:06:52,041
His body is just too thin.

1774
01:06:52,108 --> 01:06:54,310
The viewers might think

1775
01:06:54,377 --> 01:06:57,580
he messed up the dough
and got the noodles from somewhere else.

1776
01:06:57,646 --> 01:07:00,883
They won't think that.
We never lie on this show.

1777
01:07:00,950 --> 01:07:03,019
What's that? Straight into the pan?

1778
01:07:03,085 --> 01:07:04,153
Straight in?

1779
01:07:04,220 --> 01:07:06,155
What is that now?

1780
01:07:06,222 --> 01:07:08,357
-Cucumber and honey?
-Honey?

1781
01:07:08,424 --> 01:07:09,258
-Honey?
-Why?

1782
01:07:09,325 --> 01:07:13,062
He cooked the blended cucumber in a pan
and poured honey into it.

1783
01:07:13,129 --> 01:07:15,431
-The pizza dough.
-It's the dough.

1784
01:07:15,498 --> 01:07:17,333
-Will it cook?
-The whole thing?

1785
01:07:17,400 --> 01:07:19,435
It seems way too greasy.

1786
01:07:19,502 --> 01:07:21,237
-It's way too oily.
-That's the dough.

1787
01:07:21,303 --> 01:07:22,772
It's pate a choux, right?

1788
01:07:22,838 --> 01:07:25,975
It's often used to make eclairs and such.

1789
01:07:26,042 --> 01:07:27,576
Do you make pizza dough like that too?

1790
01:07:27,643 --> 01:07:28,844
-No.
-You don't do that?

1791
01:07:28,911 --> 01:07:29,779
-"No"?
-It's not that.

1792
01:07:29,845 --> 01:07:33,416
Because I have no time
to add yeast and whatnot.

1793
01:07:33,482 --> 01:07:35,951
It reminds me of potato cake.

1794
01:07:36,018 --> 01:07:39,055
I think he said
he wanted to turn it into dessert.

1795
01:07:39,121 --> 01:07:40,556
He grabs the octopus.

1796
01:07:40,623 --> 01:07:43,492
It's out. He cooked it
for exactly seven minutes,

1797
01:07:43,559 --> 01:07:45,861
spending half the time cooking that.

1798
01:07:45,928 --> 01:07:47,363
Seven minutes.

1799
01:07:47,430 --> 01:07:48,664
Seven minutes with cooking wine.

1800
01:07:48,964 --> 01:07:50,499
HO-YOUNG USES A CUCUMBER TOO

1801
01:07:50,566 --> 01:07:52,034
They're both using cucumbers.

1802
01:07:52,368 --> 01:07:54,570
SMASHED CUCUMBER SALAD
TO ACCOMPANY THE OCTOPUS!

1803
01:07:54,770 --> 01:07:57,039
CHOPPED INTO BIG PIECES

1804
01:07:57,106 --> 01:07:59,208
AND MIXED WITH VINEGAR SAUCE

1805
01:07:59,275 --> 01:08:01,577
-The noodles look great.
-The noodles.

1806
01:08:01,644 --> 01:08:03,646
-It's getting cooked.
-He actually made it.

1807
01:08:03,712 --> 01:08:06,248
It didn't suddenly appear.

1808
01:08:06,582 --> 01:08:08,284
6. COOK SQUID, SHRIMP,
ONION, AND GREEN ONION

1809
01:08:09,051 --> 01:08:10,152
What's he doing?

1810
01:08:10,219 --> 01:08:11,454
What are you doing, Poong?

1811
01:08:11,520 --> 01:08:14,557
He's punching the pizza
to keep it from rising.

1812
01:08:14,623 --> 01:08:16,325
You do that with pizza dough, right?

1813
01:08:17,760 --> 01:08:19,261
You'll pour that on top?

1814
01:08:19,328 --> 01:08:20,763
-What?
-You'll pour that?

1815
01:08:20,830 --> 01:08:22,298
Wait, that's oil.

1816
01:08:22,832 --> 01:08:24,433
-He's pouring oil on top.
-That doesn't look right.

1817
01:08:24,500 --> 01:08:25,868
-Wait.
-He's about to deep-fry it.

1818
01:08:25,935 --> 01:08:27,536
He made holes in it,
so it will probably cook.

1819
01:08:27,603 --> 01:08:29,505
That's really smart of him.

1820
01:08:29,572 --> 01:08:33,142
To prevent only the bottom part
being cooked,

1821
01:08:33,209 --> 01:08:35,311
he's heating up the top
to cook it thoroughly.

1822
01:08:35,878 --> 01:08:37,580
Like an oven.

1823
01:08:37,646 --> 01:08:41,350
Instead of flipping it,
he chose to pour oil over it.

1824
01:08:41,417 --> 01:08:42,251
LEMON JUICE

1825
01:08:42,818 --> 01:08:44,353
IS HE TRULY A GENIUS?

1826
01:08:44,420 --> 01:08:45,988
It's rising.

1827
01:08:46,856 --> 01:08:48,958
It is? It's rising.

1828
01:08:49,225 --> 01:08:53,929
5. SPREAD DOUGH IN A PAN, PUNCH,
THEN POUR HOT OIL ON TOP

1829
01:08:53,996 --> 01:08:57,566
-It's literally a high-calorie bomb.
-It looks like <i>jeon</i>.

1830
01:08:57,633 --> 01:08:59,468
Six minutes.

1831
01:08:59,535 --> 01:09:01,203
Are the noodles ready?

1832
01:09:01,470 --> 01:09:03,539
RINSE WELL-COOKED NOODLES IN COLD WATER

1833
01:09:05,441 --> 01:09:06,275
INTO THE STIR-FRY!

1834
01:09:06,342 --> 01:09:09,111
Stir-fried udon?
The texture will be amazing.

1835
01:09:09,178 --> 01:09:10,446
It looks so good.

1836
01:09:10,513 --> 01:09:12,948
So he'll do that, then put it in the oven?

1837
01:09:13,015 --> 01:09:14,450
-I guess.
-The special soy sauce.

1838
01:09:14,517 --> 01:09:15,751
7. FRY SEAFOOD, NOODLES, AND SAUCE

1839
01:09:16,819 --> 01:09:19,221
That's Ho-young's expertise.

1840
01:09:19,288 --> 01:09:20,823
LOUD ULULATION

1841
01:09:23,259 --> 01:09:25,294
ULULATION CONTINUES!

1842
01:09:25,361 --> 01:09:27,863
He wants to steal the attention.

1843
01:09:27,930 --> 01:09:31,700
-My arm hurts.
-That must be the pizza topping.

1844
01:09:31,767 --> 01:09:33,302
You're using those raw?

1845
01:09:33,369 --> 01:09:34,370
I'll pickle these.

1846
01:09:34,436 --> 01:09:36,772
-You'll pickle them?
-In five minutes?

1847
01:09:36,839 --> 01:09:38,741
That's a lot of sugar.

1848
01:09:38,807 --> 01:09:41,110
-He's pickling them in sugar.
-In sugar?

1849
01:09:41,176 --> 01:09:43,612
-And some salt too. Like pickles.
-Like pickles.

1850
01:09:43,679 --> 01:09:45,414
So it'll taste like pickles.

1851
01:09:46,215 --> 01:09:47,483
STIR-FRIED UDON, FINISHED!

1852
01:09:47,550 --> 01:09:48,951
That looks good.

1853
01:09:49,485 --> 01:09:50,319
BUTTER

1854
01:09:50,386 --> 01:09:51,220
MOZZARELLA

1855
01:09:51,287 --> 01:09:52,288
TOASTED BUCKWHEAT

1856
01:09:52,354 --> 01:09:54,857
-Jung-hwan! Please go check.
-Yes?

1857
01:09:55,591 --> 01:09:57,026
Go and have a taste.

1858
01:09:57,092 --> 01:09:58,627
Ho-young is losing attention.

1859
01:09:58,694 --> 01:10:00,396
And pollack roe? That has to be good.

1860
01:10:00,462 --> 01:10:02,464
Will he overcome his Poongphobia?

1861
01:10:02,531 --> 01:10:04,200
That has to be good.

1862
01:10:04,266 --> 01:10:06,735
-He tops it with pollack roe.
-And he'll put that in the oven?

1863
01:10:06,802 --> 01:10:09,371
It goes into the oven
with 4 minutes and 30 seconds left.

1864
01:10:09,438 --> 01:10:10,573
Four and a half minutes.

1865
01:10:10,639 --> 01:10:13,776
The pizza dough. How will this turn out?

1866
01:10:13,842 --> 01:10:16,445
Whoa, that's hot. What is this?
You're blending it?

1867
01:10:16,512 --> 01:10:18,314
-I have to blend it.
-That cream reminds me

1868
01:10:18,380 --> 01:10:21,417
-of when he made the melon fritter.
-The melon.

1869
01:10:21,483 --> 01:10:22,518
LIKE THE MELON FRITTER SAUCE?

1870
01:10:22,985 --> 01:10:24,954
It's like the melon fritter sauce?

1871
01:10:25,020 --> 01:10:28,257
On Poong's side,
it smells like a facial spa.

1872
01:10:28,324 --> 01:10:31,360
-I see.
-It reeks of cucumber.

1873
01:10:31,427 --> 01:10:32,628
A facial spa?

1874
01:10:32,695 --> 01:10:34,930
Yeo-jeong went over to look at the dough.

1875
01:10:34,997 --> 01:10:37,233
-I feel anxious about that.
-Jung-hwan, take a look at it.

1876
01:10:37,299 --> 01:10:40,569
It's currently rising,
and it's coming apart in the center.

1877
01:10:40,636 --> 01:10:43,772
-He should flip that.
-Are you sure you won't flip it?

1878
01:10:43,839 --> 01:10:45,774
BLEND AND BOIL!

1879
01:10:45,841 --> 01:10:49,011
Take your time. Be careful.

1880
01:10:49,078 --> 01:10:50,579
Use one more pan.

1881
01:10:50,646 --> 01:10:53,015
Let me use the spatula.

1882
01:10:53,082 --> 01:10:55,651
-You can use a dish.
-I can't do that here.

1883
01:10:55,718 --> 01:10:57,720
He's about to flip it.

1884
01:10:57,786 --> 01:10:59,088
HOW SWEET
WATCH OUT FOR OIL

1885
01:10:59,421 --> 01:11:01,123
WONKY

1886
01:11:01,190 --> 01:11:02,658
-No!
-No!

1887
01:11:02,725 --> 01:11:04,193
DO IT AT ONCE!

1888
01:11:04,260 --> 01:11:05,794
-Use both hands.
-At once!

1889
01:11:06,095 --> 01:11:07,396
SLIPS

1890
01:11:07,463 --> 01:11:08,998
-It slipped.
-It failed.

1891
01:11:09,064 --> 01:11:10,266
It's his second try.

1892
01:11:10,332 --> 01:11:11,667
HE FLIPPED IT!

1893
01:11:11,734 --> 01:11:12,968
RELIEVED

1894
01:11:13,035 --> 01:11:14,303
ANXIOUS FEET

1895
01:11:14,370 --> 01:11:15,404
CLAPPING

1896
01:11:15,471 --> 01:11:18,741
-I got it.
-It looks like <i>hotteok.</i> It should be good.

1897
01:11:18,807 --> 01:11:21,310
-It's like the crunchy balloon bread.
-I see.

1898
01:11:21,810 --> 01:11:23,812
LEMON

1899
01:11:24,280 --> 01:11:26,582
ADDING LEMON JUICE TO THE VINEGAR SAUCE

1900
01:11:27,783 --> 01:11:29,218
AND THE LONG-AWAITED STEP!

1901
01:11:29,285 --> 01:11:31,887
-There's the octopus.
-The octopus.

1902
01:11:31,954 --> 01:11:33,889
-It looks tender.
-Yes.

1903
01:11:33,956 --> 01:11:35,524
-Jung-hwan.
-After seven minutes. Yes?

1904
01:11:35,591 --> 01:11:37,893
Try a piece of the octopus.

1905
01:11:37,960 --> 01:11:39,228
Do you have any sauce?

1906
01:11:39,295 --> 01:11:40,963
T-t-there. The vinegar…

1907
01:11:41,030 --> 01:11:42,698
See how well it's cooked.

1908
01:11:42,765 --> 01:11:45,334
-Let me dip it in the sauce.
-Sure.

1909
01:11:45,401 --> 01:11:46,969
-What's the octopus like?
-The octopus.

1910
01:11:47,036 --> 01:11:48,203
He cooked it for seven minutes.

1911
01:11:48,437 --> 01:11:49,538
OCTOPUS♥

1912
01:11:49,605 --> 01:11:53,242
Is it cooked perfectly enough
to let him get over Poongphobia?

1913
01:11:53,309 --> 01:11:54,443
What's it like?

1914
01:11:55,010 --> 01:11:56,412
Is it cooked well?

1915
01:11:57,279 --> 01:11:58,881
No, right? Is it still tough?

1916
01:11:58,947 --> 01:12:00,215
-Emergency.
-Is it tough?

1917
01:12:00,282 --> 01:12:01,984
That can happen with octopus.

1918
01:12:02,051 --> 01:12:04,019
He can only escape halfway.

1919
01:12:04,720 --> 01:12:06,055
It's a bit tough.

1920
01:12:06,121 --> 01:12:07,222
He made cuts right away.

1921
01:12:07,289 --> 01:12:08,857
It may be because I had a thick portion.

1922
01:12:08,924 --> 01:12:11,226
-It'll be different if it's thin.
-What now?

1923
01:12:11,293 --> 01:12:12,594
-Will it turn okay over time?
-I made cuts.

1924
01:12:12,661 --> 01:12:15,264
-It's fine.
-He made really thin slices.

1925
01:12:15,331 --> 01:12:17,499
-But I had the thick tip.
-At the end,

1926
01:12:17,566 --> 01:12:20,235
he made some cuts into it,
so it should be fine.

1927
01:12:20,302 --> 01:12:21,503
Mine didn't have cuts.

1928
01:12:21,570 --> 01:12:24,340
Starch.

1929
01:12:25,040 --> 01:12:26,675
He's using starch?

1930
01:12:26,742 --> 01:12:29,211
Wait, he called it a cream,
but he's making it thick with starch.

1931
01:12:29,278 --> 01:12:31,814
Jung-hwan, that cucumber cream.

1932
01:12:31,880 --> 01:12:33,982
-The cucumber thing.
-What's boiling here?

1933
01:12:34,049 --> 01:12:36,652
-Two minutes.
-So this is the topping, right?

1934
01:12:36,719 --> 01:12:38,987
-Yes.
-The topping… It looks hot.

1935
01:12:39,054 --> 01:12:40,789
I wonder what that's like.

1936
01:12:40,856 --> 01:12:42,391
-Cucumber.
-Is it just like a cucumber?

1937
01:12:42,458 --> 01:12:45,427
I hope Princess Yeo-jeong likes it.

1938
01:12:45,494 --> 01:12:48,897
Does it taste like
something Her Highness would love?

1939
01:12:48,964 --> 01:12:50,165
Whoa.

1940
01:12:50,232 --> 01:12:51,333
She'd love this!

1941
01:12:52,668 --> 01:12:54,236
-It's sweet.
-Really?

1942
01:12:54,303 --> 01:12:55,637
It's sweet?

1943
01:12:55,704 --> 01:12:56,739
I can't believe it.

1944
01:12:56,805 --> 01:12:58,407
The cucumber flavor isn't too strong.

1945
01:12:58,474 --> 01:13:00,442
-I see.
-It's there, though.

1946
01:13:00,509 --> 01:13:02,211
It must taste like melons.

1947
01:13:02,277 --> 01:13:05,714
Yes, it reminds me of melons,
and the texture is like grated potatoes.

1948
01:13:06,548 --> 01:13:08,417
It turned out nicely.

1949
01:13:08,484 --> 01:13:10,386
One minute.

1950
01:13:10,452 --> 01:13:13,155
Octopus with vinegar sauce.

1951
01:13:13,222 --> 01:13:14,757
Octopus with vinegar sauce

1952
01:13:14,823 --> 01:13:16,859
-and lemon.
-Hurry up.

1953
01:13:16,925 --> 01:13:18,026
Lemon zest.

1954
01:13:18,093 --> 01:13:21,230
-Under one minute.
-That looks good.

1955
01:13:21,296 --> 01:13:22,131
It looks good.

1956
01:13:22,197 --> 01:13:24,066
-Poong's dish looks good.
-It does.

1957
01:13:24,133 --> 01:13:25,868
-My gosh.
-Hurry up.

1958
01:13:25,934 --> 01:13:27,636
Try a little harder, Ho-young.

1959
01:13:27,703 --> 01:13:29,304
That looks so good.

1960
01:13:29,371 --> 01:13:31,807
He pulled out the udon
with 30 seconds left.

1961
01:13:31,874 --> 01:13:33,776
I can see pollack roe and cheese.

1962
01:13:34,777 --> 01:13:35,611
The torch.

1963
01:13:35,677 --> 01:13:36,845
-Did you use ricotta?
-Not yet.

1964
01:13:36,912 --> 01:13:38,046
-What's that?
-Garlic.

1965
01:13:38,113 --> 01:13:40,048
-Garlic?
-Garlic in a dessert?

1966
01:13:40,115 --> 01:13:41,784
She doesn't really like it.

1967
01:13:41,850 --> 01:13:43,886
No, it's okay. I can eat it.

1968
01:13:43,952 --> 01:13:46,688
-He's using just the juice.
-A tiny dash.

1969
01:13:47,289 --> 01:13:49,258
-Twenty-five seconds.
-Twenty seconds.

1970
01:13:49,324 --> 01:13:50,159
He's almost done.

1971
01:13:50,225 --> 01:13:52,027
Time to wrap up. Twenty seconds.

1972
01:13:52,094 --> 01:13:53,529
-Hurry up.
-Twenty seconds.

1973
01:13:54,263 --> 01:13:55,931
-Twenty seconds.
-He wrings the cucumber slices.

1974
01:13:55,998 --> 01:13:58,467
-Poong… No, Ho-young is done.
-Ho-young finished first.

1975
01:13:58,534 --> 01:14:00,369
POONG BEGINS TO PLATE HIS DISH TOO!

1976
01:14:00,436 --> 01:14:01,670
It's hot.

1977
01:14:01,737 --> 01:14:03,939
Poong, put the toppings on the pizza.

1978
01:14:04,006 --> 01:14:04,840
Ten.

1979
01:14:04,907 --> 01:14:05,841
-Nine.
-Nine.

1980
01:14:05,908 --> 01:14:06,775
-Eight.
-Eight.

1981
01:14:06,842 --> 01:14:07,810
-Seven.
-Seven.

1982
01:14:07,876 --> 01:14:09,044
-Six.
-Six.

1983
01:14:09,211 --> 01:14:10,712
DROPPING A TON OF CUCUMBER CREAM

1984
01:14:11,046 --> 01:14:13,248
AND TOPS IT WITH PICKLES!

1985
01:14:13,315 --> 01:14:14,216
-Four.
-Four.

1986
01:14:14,283 --> 01:14:15,250
-Three.
-Three.

1987
01:14:15,317 --> 01:14:17,152
-Two. The end.
-Two. One.

1988
01:14:17,219 --> 01:14:18,520
It's over.

1989
01:14:18,587 --> 01:14:20,088
-Time's up, Poong.
-All right.

1990
01:14:20,456 --> 01:14:21,757
YOU TRIED…

1991
01:14:21,824 --> 01:14:23,959
-What about ricotta?
-Where's the cheese?

1992
01:14:24,026 --> 01:14:25,994
-Can I put this on top?
-Ask Ho-young.

1993
01:14:26,061 --> 01:14:28,063
It's not my call.

1994
01:14:28,130 --> 01:14:30,299
-Ask him.
-May I top this just a little?

1995
01:14:30,365 --> 01:14:31,700
Just serve it together.

1996
01:14:31,767 --> 01:14:33,168
-Right.
-Serve it on the side.

1997
01:14:33,235 --> 01:14:34,670
-You're a genius.
-Yes.

1998
01:14:34,736 --> 01:14:36,205
-On the side.
-Just serve that.

1999
01:14:36,271 --> 01:14:38,240
-On the side.
-It looks kind of classy.

2000
01:14:38,307 --> 01:14:39,808
She can top it when she eats it.

2001
01:14:39,875 --> 01:14:41,510
-He's so smart.
-Serve it on the side.

2002
01:14:41,577 --> 01:14:45,214
KIM POONG FINISHES MAKING
PIZZA NATION, PRINCESS YEO-JEONG

2003
01:14:45,280 --> 01:14:47,416
It looks cool too.

2004
01:14:47,483 --> 01:14:49,451
-It's a creative presentation.
-Poong is done too.

2005
01:14:50,819 --> 01:14:52,621
It's so creative.

2006
01:14:53,021 --> 01:14:54,556
DELICIOUSLY PRESENTED

2007
01:14:55,491 --> 01:14:57,326
-My gosh.
-Yes.

2008
01:14:57,392 --> 01:15:00,762
Everything has been prepared
for Yeo-jeong.

2009
01:15:00,829 --> 01:15:03,532
Unlike the first round,

2010
01:15:03,599 --> 01:15:06,068
<i>she was a bit more worried,</i>
<i>and she even went closer to look.</i>

2011
01:15:06,134 --> 01:15:07,970
Were you quite worried about Poong's dish?

2012
01:15:08,670 --> 01:15:12,074
I was surprised
to see the deep-fried dough.

2013
01:15:12,140 --> 01:15:15,577
She wasn't sure
if she could actually eat it,

2014
01:15:15,644 --> 01:15:17,312
so she had to go see it for herself.

2015
01:15:17,379 --> 01:15:20,215
Ho-young finished first,

2016
01:15:20,282 --> 01:15:23,118
so please try
Walk Pollack Roely Anywhere You Go.

2017
01:15:24,086 --> 01:15:27,689
SWEET AND SOUR OCTOPUS SALAD
& STIR-FRIED UDON

2018
01:15:29,024 --> 01:15:33,295
FULL OF POLLACK ROE AND CHEESE

2019
01:15:35,998 --> 01:15:38,901
CHEF JUNG HO-YOUNG'S
WALK POLLACK ROELY ANYWHERE YOU GO

2020
01:15:39,201 --> 01:15:40,903
AMAZED

2021
01:15:41,136 --> 01:15:44,373
-It looks so good.
-Ho-young desperately wants a star too.

2022
01:15:44,439 --> 01:15:47,476
-That's why he made what he's best at.
-His specialty.

2023
01:15:47,543 --> 01:15:49,077
There's cucumber too.

2024
01:15:49,144 --> 01:15:51,847
She puts her self-discipline behind.

2025
01:15:51,914 --> 01:15:52,948
It looks so good.

2026
01:15:53,015 --> 01:15:57,219
Octopus is all about how well it's cooked.

2027
01:15:57,286 --> 01:15:58,820
Have a piece of cucumber too.

2028
01:15:58,887 --> 01:16:00,088
SO?

2029
01:16:00,155 --> 01:16:01,590
It's like an appetizer.

2030
01:16:01,657 --> 01:16:02,891
NODDING

2031
01:16:02,958 --> 01:16:05,227
So you have to cook it to this level.

2032
01:16:05,294 --> 01:16:07,229
-Is it cooked well?
-That's how. Yes.

2033
01:16:07,296 --> 01:16:08,564
-It's not tough?
-No.

2034
01:16:09,197 --> 01:16:11,967
-It's good.
-She says it's good.

2035
01:16:13,201 --> 01:16:15,537
I want to know the recipe. Soy sauce…

2036
01:16:15,604 --> 01:16:19,441
It's simple. Two parts soy sauce, one
vinegar, one sugar, and one lemon juice.

2037
01:16:19,508 --> 01:16:21,710
What about the red powder?

2038
01:16:21,777 --> 01:16:23,679
I sprinkled some red pepper powder.

2039
01:16:24,680 --> 01:16:26,315
<i>It's spicy, sour, salty,</i>

2040
01:16:26,381 --> 01:16:28,917
-and sweet. Every flavor.
-It has all kinds of flavors.

2041
01:16:28,984 --> 01:16:30,719
Because I eat lots of seafood,

2042
01:16:30,786 --> 01:16:32,354
I end up getting a bit sick of it.

2043
01:16:32,421 --> 01:16:35,791
But this dash of red pepper powder
adds a nice twist.

2044
01:16:36,024 --> 01:16:38,026
THAT'S WHY I DID IT

2045
01:16:38,727 --> 01:16:40,228
Next, the udon.

2046
01:16:40,295 --> 01:16:41,830
Oh, that udon looks so good.

2047
01:16:42,531 --> 01:16:45,000
-It looks so good. What do I do?
-I want to try it so bad.

2048
01:16:45,067 --> 01:16:47,469
-The Japanese pub style.
-Stir-fried udon.

2049
01:16:47,536 --> 01:16:49,237
And baked in the oven, too.

2050
01:16:49,304 --> 01:16:50,272
STRETCH

2051
01:16:50,339 --> 01:16:53,241
-My gosh.
-Look at how much cheese there is.

2052
01:16:53,308 --> 01:16:54,176
I can't say no to that.

2053
01:16:54,242 --> 01:16:55,243
Look at that cheese.

2054
01:16:55,310 --> 01:16:56,778
A CHEESE BOMB

2055
01:16:56,845 --> 01:16:58,747
There's more cheese than I thought.

2056
01:16:58,814 --> 01:17:00,749
-It looks so good.
-Yes.

2057
01:17:00,816 --> 01:17:02,618
You can probably play
tug-of-war with that.

2058
01:17:03,619 --> 01:17:04,987
YOU'RE HILARIOUS

2059
01:17:06,254 --> 01:17:07,656
She ate that in one bite.

2060
01:17:08,590 --> 01:17:09,558
SLURP

2061
01:17:10,659 --> 01:17:12,861
-It must've been forever.
-It looks good.

2062
01:17:14,329 --> 01:17:15,530
And the noodles.

2063
01:17:15,597 --> 01:17:16,898
The noodles are so good.

2064
01:17:16,965 --> 01:17:18,600
Is it? It must've turned out nicely.

2065
01:17:19,901 --> 01:17:21,837
FRESH UDON NOODLES ARE PERFECT

2066
01:17:21,903 --> 01:17:24,640
We didn't see the noodles being made
because of Jong-won.

2067
01:17:25,874 --> 01:17:27,542
You made it, right?

2068
01:17:27,609 --> 01:17:30,345
-I did.
-Many viewers are skeptical.

2069
01:17:30,412 --> 01:17:33,515
<i>Did Jong-won block the camera</i>
<i>while you swapped out the noodles?</i>

2070
01:17:33,582 --> 01:17:36,251
-I think he opened a bag.
-It can't look that good.

2071
01:17:36,318 --> 01:17:38,887
You made that? Why does it look so good?

2072
01:17:38,954 --> 01:17:40,288
-I'm suspicious.
-I don't know.

2073
01:17:41,556 --> 01:17:44,493
-I want a big bite of noodles.
-A big bite of noodles.

2074
01:17:44,559 --> 01:17:46,161
She wants a big bite of noodles.

2075
01:17:46,228 --> 01:17:48,730
-Great news for Ho-young.
-She's enjoying it.

2076
01:17:48,797 --> 01:17:49,831
I want some too.

2077
01:17:49,898 --> 01:17:52,668
-She knows how to eat noodles.
-I can't take it anymore.

2078
01:17:52,734 --> 01:17:53,769
She controls herself.

2079
01:17:53,835 --> 01:17:55,971
She eats like this
only once or twice a year.

2080
01:17:56,838 --> 01:17:59,541
-It's so good.
-She loves it,

2081
01:17:59,608 --> 01:18:01,043
yet she can't have it too often.

2082
01:18:01,109 --> 01:18:03,545
This is so heartbreaking.

2083
01:18:03,612 --> 01:18:07,816
It's my first time
trying freshly made udon noodles.

2084
01:18:07,883 --> 01:18:09,651
It's the best stir-fried udon of my life.

2085
01:18:09,718 --> 01:18:11,253
BEST STIR-FRIED UDON OF HER LIFE

2086
01:18:11,319 --> 01:18:12,387
It's so good.

2087
01:18:12,454 --> 01:18:16,358
It also has lots of seafood that I love,

2088
01:18:16,425 --> 01:18:20,829
so I'm close to forgetting
this guilt over eating flour.

2089
01:18:20,896 --> 01:18:22,764
The seafood is great.

2090
01:18:22,831 --> 01:18:24,900
-Because it's abundant?
-Yes, and it's good.

2091
01:18:24,966 --> 01:18:28,103
-It's so good.
-She looks quite pleased.

2092
01:18:28,170 --> 01:18:30,706
And a piece of cucumber, like a side dish.

2093
01:18:32,841 --> 01:18:34,876
-It's so good.
-Was it good? Excellent.

2094
01:18:34,943 --> 01:18:37,646
-Next.
-Now, the dish in question.

2095
01:18:37,713 --> 01:18:39,948
-Poong's cucumber pizza.
-The dessert.

2096
01:18:42,417 --> 01:18:45,987
CUCUMBER PIZZA

2097
01:18:47,189 --> 01:18:51,393
DEEP-FRIED DOUGH AND SWEET CUCUMBER CREAM

2098
01:18:53,729 --> 01:18:58,133
WEBTOON ARTIST KIM POONG'S
PIZZA NATION, PRINCESS YEO-JEONG

2099
01:18:58,200 --> 01:19:01,670
He only makes pizza
for those who represent the nation,

2100
01:19:01,737 --> 01:19:03,572
and he made one for you.

2101
01:19:03,638 --> 01:19:05,474
I just brought extra cream.

2102
01:19:05,540 --> 01:19:08,677
-Wait, you can't just bring that here.
-Wait, hear me out.

2103
01:19:08,744 --> 01:19:10,345
Why are you adding stuff?

2104
01:19:10,412 --> 01:19:12,481
It's the same cucumber cream.

2105
01:19:12,547 --> 01:19:15,217
It's the same thing?
If you want more, add some more.

2106
01:19:15,283 --> 01:19:17,886
-I don't know how she'd like it, so…
-Yes, sure.

2107
01:19:17,953 --> 01:19:20,222
-It was intentional.
-That was why, right?

2108
01:19:20,288 --> 01:19:23,992
-It's not that you ran out of time?
-It's not that.

2109
01:19:24,760 --> 01:19:26,728
IT'S SAFE(?)

2110
01:19:26,795 --> 01:19:29,264
This looks more like cucumber jam.

2111
01:19:29,331 --> 01:19:33,568
The dough is different from regular pizza.

2112
01:19:33,635 --> 01:19:37,305
It's rather greasy,
so I wonder if that'll be too much.

2113
01:19:37,372 --> 01:19:38,607
And…

2114
01:19:38,673 --> 01:19:40,542
I'd like lots of cucumber slices.

2115
01:19:40,609 --> 01:19:43,311
-Lots of cucumber slices.
-No, this one, with lots of jam too.

2116
01:19:43,378 --> 01:19:44,212
I'm getting greedy.

2117
01:19:44,279 --> 01:19:47,516
I'm feeling gluttonous.
Lots of cucumber and jam.

2118
01:19:48,750 --> 01:19:51,853
-He's serving a piece.
-Thank you.

2119
01:19:52,521 --> 01:19:53,522
Thank you.

2120
01:19:53,588 --> 01:19:54,956
EVEN THE HOSTS FIND IT FASCINATING

2121
01:19:55,023 --> 01:19:57,993
-Try it as is, without anything else.
-Okay.

2122
01:19:58,059 --> 01:19:59,528
NOM

2123
01:20:00,662 --> 01:20:01,496
WHAT'S IT LIKE?

2124
01:20:01,563 --> 01:20:03,698
She carefully took a bite.

2125
01:20:05,267 --> 01:20:08,470
SMILING

2126
01:20:08,870 --> 01:20:10,672
WHAT DOES HER SMILE MEAN?

2127
01:20:10,739 --> 01:20:12,741
She hasn't made a comment yet.

2128
01:20:12,808 --> 01:20:14,543
-It must be sweet.
-No comment.

2129
01:20:14,609 --> 01:20:16,077
She might swear at him.

2130
01:20:16,545 --> 01:20:18,013
INSTEAD, ADDS RICOTTA

2131
01:20:18,079 --> 01:20:18,914
"Darn it."

2132
01:20:18,980 --> 01:20:20,715
That might be too much.

2133
01:20:20,782 --> 01:20:22,217
She should add lots.

2134
01:20:22,284 --> 01:20:23,451
A spoonful of ricotta.

2135
01:20:23,518 --> 01:20:26,321
If she adds too much,
she won't taste the cucumber.

2136
01:20:26,388 --> 01:20:29,024
Her facial expression doesn't look bad.

2137
01:20:29,090 --> 01:20:31,760
How will it change with ricotta?

2138
01:20:31,827 --> 01:20:33,228
I'll probably look awful.

2139
01:20:34,596 --> 01:20:37,365
Does she have to eat it like this?

2140
01:20:37,432 --> 01:20:39,334
Must Her Highness eat it like this?

2141
01:20:40,101 --> 01:20:41,670
Lock up that man.

2142
01:20:42,237 --> 01:20:44,840
-And flog him.
-How dare he do this to Her Highness?

2143
01:20:44,906 --> 01:20:47,776
-Yes.
-Lock up Kim Poong.

2144
01:20:47,843 --> 01:20:50,946
-Let me try it like this.
-Dip it in the cream.

2145
01:20:51,012 --> 01:20:53,548
It felt like cucumber jam when I tried it.

2146
01:20:53,615 --> 01:20:54,449
Mmm.

2147
01:20:54,649 --> 01:20:55,684
HUH?

2148
01:20:55,750 --> 01:20:57,452
This cucumber jam is really good.

2149
01:20:57,519 --> 01:20:59,287
I keep calling it jam.

2150
01:20:59,354 --> 01:21:00,922
What did you add in here?

2151
01:21:00,989 --> 01:21:05,327
Peeled cucumber, then sugar or honey,
and lastly, butter.

2152
01:21:05,393 --> 01:21:07,395
That's it. And starch.

2153
01:21:07,462 --> 01:21:09,264
And did you boil it?

2154
01:21:09,331 --> 01:21:13,235
<i>Yes, I boiled it,</i>
<i>then made it thicker with starch.</i>

2155
01:21:13,301 --> 01:21:14,970
-Is she…
-This is odd.

2156
01:21:15,036 --> 01:21:17,606
…smiling because it's good?

2157
01:21:17,672 --> 01:21:20,008
Or because it's funny?

2158
01:21:20,075 --> 01:21:22,677
-We can't tell.
-She either loves it or hates it.

2159
01:21:23,245 --> 01:21:25,046
I wouldn't call this pizza.

2160
01:21:25,113 --> 01:21:27,649
-It has to be.
-It's more like a rich confectionery.

2161
01:21:27,716 --> 01:21:28,650
Confectionery?

2162
01:21:28,717 --> 01:21:31,353
The dough is similar to churros dough.

2163
01:21:31,419 --> 01:21:33,588
Yes, it's like churros.

2164
01:21:33,655 --> 01:21:35,457
But do you know what's odd?

2165
01:21:36,758 --> 01:21:39,194
I find myself keep going back for it.

2166
01:21:39,261 --> 01:21:40,462
What's with this?

2167
01:21:40,528 --> 01:21:41,930
-Do you keep reaching out for it?
-Yes.

2168
01:21:41,997 --> 01:21:43,098
Why is that?

2169
01:21:43,164 --> 01:21:44,432
It'd be weird if you used your feet.

2170
01:21:45,967 --> 01:21:48,236
OH…

2171
01:21:48,303 --> 01:21:50,238
-Turn that on.
-That was funny.

2172
01:21:50,305 --> 01:21:51,273
Why? It was funny.

2173
01:21:51,339 --> 01:21:53,675
-Turn it on.
-She keeps reaching for it.

2174
01:21:53,742 --> 01:21:57,245
At my favorite pizza joint,

2175
01:21:57,312 --> 01:22:00,382
they have dessert pizzas

2176
01:22:00,448 --> 01:22:02,617
-made with blueberries and cream cheese.
-Or chocolate.

2177
01:22:02,684 --> 01:22:06,688
It's like another dessert pizza
that's on the menu.

2178
01:22:06,755 --> 01:22:08,189
That was what I intended.

2179
01:22:08,256 --> 01:22:11,826
Please try Chef Ho-young's dish first.

2180
01:22:15,063 --> 01:22:18,800
-Did he chop the pollack roe?
-It's because she loves noodles.

2181
01:22:19,100 --> 01:22:20,835
NODDING

2182
01:22:20,902 --> 01:22:24,306
There's a bit of smoky flavor
on the pollack roe.

2183
01:22:24,372 --> 01:22:26,875
And that helps me keep eating
without getting sick of it.

2184
01:22:26,942 --> 01:22:29,144
I finished it.

2185
01:22:29,210 --> 01:22:30,345
And I wasn't even hungry.

2186
01:22:30,412 --> 01:22:32,347
You ate the rest all alone?

2187
01:22:32,414 --> 01:22:34,549
I thought the noodles would fail,

2188
01:22:34,616 --> 01:22:36,351
but the finished product

2189
01:22:36,418 --> 01:22:39,521
looks even and nice
like store-bought noodles.

2190
01:22:39,587 --> 01:22:41,289
I couldn't quite see it.

2191
01:22:41,356 --> 01:22:44,960
Did you cut the noodles
after you flattened it?

2192
01:22:45,026 --> 01:22:47,796
The same machine cuts the noodles too.

2193
01:22:47,862 --> 01:22:49,431
Even Yeo-jeong is suspicious.

2194
01:22:49,497 --> 01:22:51,666
-They may have switched it out.
-No, wait.

2195
01:22:51,733 --> 01:22:54,469
When did he chop the noodles
after flattening the dough?

2196
01:22:54,536 --> 01:22:55,503
<i>I really didn't see it.</i>

2197
01:22:55,570 --> 01:22:57,372
ARE YOU WATCHING THIS ON TV, YEO-JEONG?

2198
01:22:57,439 --> 01:22:59,641
<i>We should've seen it,</i>
<i>but Jong-won's head blocked it.</i>

2199
01:22:59,708 --> 01:23:01,609
INNOCENT

2200
01:23:01,676 --> 01:23:03,345
Next, Poong's dish.

2201
01:23:03,912 --> 01:23:06,047
-This is odd.
-How will you feel about it?

2202
01:23:06,114 --> 01:23:07,215
Be honest.

2203
01:23:07,282 --> 01:23:09,351
Let's share our opinions honestly.

2204
01:23:09,584 --> 01:23:10,418
WHAT'S IT LIKE, EVERYONE?

2205
01:23:10,485 --> 01:23:11,886
It's either love it or hate it.

2206
01:23:12,454 --> 01:23:13,922
I see why he used garlic.

2207
01:23:13,989 --> 01:23:15,657
INHALES

2208
01:23:15,724 --> 01:23:16,791
At the end…

2209
01:23:16,858 --> 01:23:17,692
2 HITS

2210
01:23:18,159 --> 01:23:18,994
3 HITS

2211
01:23:20,762 --> 01:23:22,130
UNSURE?

2212
01:23:22,597 --> 01:23:24,699
This has a cute flavor to it.

2213
01:23:24,766 --> 01:23:26,601
-I see.
-Isn't it intriguing?

2214
01:23:26,668 --> 01:23:29,204
This would be a great dish to feed kids

2215
01:23:29,270 --> 01:23:31,906
who don't like cucumbers.

2216
01:23:31,973 --> 01:23:35,010
It's not too complicated.
There's no need to analyze this.

2217
01:23:35,076 --> 01:23:37,979
Also, that slight dash of garlic

2218
01:23:38,046 --> 01:23:41,149
works very well with me. That single dash.

2219
01:23:41,216 --> 01:23:43,418
There's a confectionery snack called

2220
01:23:43,485 --> 01:23:44,452
French Pie.

2221
01:23:44,953 --> 01:23:47,889
-That's it. French Pie.
-It felt like I was eating that.

2222
01:23:47,956 --> 01:23:51,559
It brought back great memories,
and crunchy cucumber added a good texture.

2223
01:23:51,626 --> 01:23:54,462
-Like French Pie.
-The ones with apple flavor and such.

2224
01:23:54,529 --> 01:23:57,432
This pizza reminds me of my childhood.

2225
01:23:57,499 --> 01:24:00,702
My grandma had a perilla leaf farm.

2226
01:24:01,436 --> 01:24:02,971
-What?
-Back to the farm?

2227
01:24:03,038 --> 01:24:04,873
And the neighboring granny
had a cucumber farm.

2228
01:24:06,374 --> 01:24:09,377
I fell asleep there
while playing hide-and-seek,

2229
01:24:09,444 --> 01:24:11,446
then woke up in the Mediterranean.

2230
01:24:11,813 --> 01:24:15,550
A JOURNEY TO THE MEDITERRANEAN
FROM HIS GRANDMA'S NEIGHBOR'S FARM

2231
01:24:15,617 --> 01:24:20,355
The mixture of cucumber and ricotta
is a very Mediterranean way of eating.

2232
01:24:20,422 --> 01:24:22,624
We should call this Greek pizza.

2233
01:24:22,690 --> 01:24:24,726
Actual Greeks will be mad
when they see this.

2234
01:24:24,793 --> 01:24:27,395
That was an excellent comparison.

2235
01:24:27,462 --> 01:24:28,296
Thank you.

2236
01:24:28,363 --> 01:24:29,597
It's very delicious.

2237
01:24:29,664 --> 01:24:32,801
And this familiar balance
isn't so bad either.

2238
01:24:32,867 --> 01:24:35,437
But if he wanted to add
a little more impact,

2239
01:24:35,503 --> 01:24:37,405
he could've salted the dough.

2240
01:24:37,472 --> 01:24:39,941
Then it would've been perfect.

2241
01:24:40,008 --> 01:24:41,976
You should've told him.

2242
01:24:42,043 --> 01:24:44,646
I had no idea what he was up to.

2243
01:24:44,712 --> 01:24:47,082
Exactly. He thought he'd manage.

2244
01:24:47,148 --> 01:24:49,684
-The biggest eater, Nam-no.
-Nam-no.

2245
01:24:49,751 --> 01:24:52,454
-Time to earn your keep.
-This isn't a buffet.

2246
01:24:52,520 --> 01:24:55,857
Why do we always give him
multiple servings?

2247
01:24:55,924 --> 01:24:57,759
What's that salt doing here?

2248
01:24:57,826 --> 01:25:00,628
I tried it with salt as he suggested.

2249
01:25:00,695 --> 01:25:03,031
After a bit of salt on the cucumber pizza,

2250
01:25:03,098 --> 01:25:04,432
the flavor became brighter.

2251
01:25:04,499 --> 01:25:06,434
You tried it right away?

2252
01:25:06,768 --> 01:25:09,904
ALWAYS QUICK TO ACT WHEN IT COMES TO FOOD

2253
01:25:09,971 --> 01:25:14,776
-It's like Greek salad. Feta and cucumber.
-Greek salad?

2254
01:25:14,843 --> 01:25:17,112
But it had been made by a Chinese man.

2255
01:25:17,178 --> 01:25:20,014
-It has that Chinese bread flavor.
-It does.

2256
01:25:20,081 --> 01:25:22,584
It's like the thin wheat crêpes.

2257
01:25:22,650 --> 01:25:24,819
A Chinese man residing in Greece?

2258
01:25:24,886 --> 01:25:27,522
-A Chinese man in Greece?
-A Chinese man in Greece?

2259
01:25:27,589 --> 01:25:29,524
POONG MAKES IT HAPPEN

2260
01:25:29,591 --> 01:25:31,493
-It's time to choose.
-Yes.

2261
01:25:31,559 --> 01:25:33,394
The choice is Yeo-jeong's.

2262
01:25:33,461 --> 01:25:34,963
<i>Press one for Ho-young</i>

2263
01:25:35,597 --> 01:25:36,798
<i>and two for Poong.</i>

2264
01:25:37,765 --> 01:25:40,435
Make your decision and press one button!

2265
01:25:41,536 --> 01:25:43,271
-I did.
-You did?

2266
01:25:43,338 --> 01:25:44,939
She makes it so quick.

2267
01:25:45,006 --> 01:25:47,675
She makes a quick decision
with a smile on her face.

2268
01:25:47,742 --> 01:25:50,445
Ho-young looks rather anxious.

2269
01:25:50,512 --> 01:25:52,614
-He's in a losing streak.
-Four losses against Poong.

2270
01:25:52,680 --> 01:25:54,482
Let's see the result.

2271
01:25:54,549 --> 01:25:56,117
-Show us.
-Yeo-jeong's choice.

2272
01:25:56,184 --> 01:25:58,553
Self-Discipline Was Just the Beginning.

2273
01:25:58,620 --> 01:26:01,656
Will Poong prove himself again
to be strong against Ho-young?

2274
01:26:01,723 --> 01:26:04,559
Or will Ho-young get his revenge?

2275
01:26:05,059 --> 01:26:07,896
Who did she choose?

2276
01:26:07,962 --> 01:26:10,331
Who's the winner?

2277
01:26:10,398 --> 01:26:12,734
Yeo-jeong's choice!

2278
01:26:12,967 --> 01:26:14,235
JUNG HO-YOUNG WINS

2279
01:26:14,302 --> 01:26:15,770
Jung Ho-young.

2280
01:26:15,970 --> 01:26:18,473
CHEF JUNG HO-YOUNG'S
WALK POLLACK ROELY ANYWHERE YOU GO WINS

2281
01:26:19,174 --> 01:26:21,242
Ho-young breaks his losing streak.

2282
01:26:22,577 --> 01:26:25,680
He got his revenge on Poong.

2283
01:26:25,747 --> 01:26:27,382
When people eat something fatty,

2284
01:26:27,448 --> 01:26:29,717
they joke, "The food is fatty, not me."

2285
01:26:29,784 --> 01:26:32,520
And I don't like doing that
because it sounds like an excuse.

2286
01:26:32,587 --> 01:26:33,688
But when I had this,

2287
01:26:33,755 --> 01:26:36,424
it made me want to go,
"Whatever. I didn't eat any noodles."

2288
01:26:36,491 --> 01:26:37,325
It felt like that.

2289
01:26:37,392 --> 01:26:40,562
-You only had seafood.
-Yes, like, "I only had seafood."

2290
01:26:40,628 --> 01:26:42,063
I wanted to do that from time to time.

2291
01:26:42,130 --> 01:26:44,432
I feel small and lose my confidence

2292
01:26:44,499 --> 01:26:47,235
whenever I lose to Poong,
as opposed to other chefs.

2293
01:26:47,302 --> 01:26:49,737
-Yes, seriously.
-So through this victory,

2294
01:26:49,804 --> 01:26:52,473
I got to recover a bit of confidence.

2295
01:26:52,540 --> 01:26:54,475
-Thank you so much.
-Right?

2296
01:26:54,542 --> 01:26:57,178
You can walk back home triumphantly today.

2297
01:26:57,245 --> 01:26:59,547
Please put a star on Chef Ho-young.

2298
01:27:00,114 --> 01:27:01,783
It's his seventh star, seventh win!

2299
01:27:01,849 --> 01:27:03,651
-It was delicious.
-Ho-young!

2300
01:27:03,718 --> 01:27:06,120
He can now walk confidently.
Congratulations!

2301
01:27:06,187 --> 01:27:07,422
Ho-young's seventh win!

2302
01:27:08,890 --> 01:27:10,658
An engineering major
and an intellectual heartthrob.

2303
01:27:10,725 --> 01:27:12,527
We probably studied
a few similar subjects.

2304
01:27:12,594 --> 01:27:13,595
I also attended a vo-tech school.

2305
01:27:13,661 --> 01:27:16,331
PRESENTING
THE INTELLECTUAL HEARTTHROB'S FRIDGE!

2306
01:27:16,397 --> 01:27:18,032
The ones that arrive early go to the back.

2307
01:27:18,099 --> 01:27:19,367
First-in, first-out.

2308
01:27:19,434 --> 01:27:20,401
I'm in a state of hyperarousal…

2309
01:27:20,568 --> 01:27:21,536
HIS ENGINEER BRAIN

2310
01:27:21,603 --> 01:27:23,137
I hear you talk to yourself often.

2311
01:27:23,204 --> 01:27:24,505
I find myself mumbling.

2312
01:27:24,572 --> 01:27:25,607
"What's in the fridge?"

2313
01:27:25,673 --> 01:27:27,275
"The traffic is heavy."

2314
01:27:27,475 --> 01:27:28,643
THE OLD ENGINEERING MAJOR DUDE(?)

2315
01:27:28,977 --> 01:27:30,545
ASKS FOR A SOUP DISH ROUND

2316
01:27:30,845 --> 01:27:32,714
THE KIND OF SOUP HE'LL LOVE

2317
01:27:32,914 --> 01:27:33,881
RED RED

2318
01:27:33,948 --> 01:27:34,782
IT LOOKS SO GOOD

2319
01:27:34,849 --> 01:27:36,217
Old man, come and hold this.

2320
01:27:36,284 --> 01:27:37,485
THE OLD DUDE IS HERE

2321
01:27:37,752 --> 01:27:38,820
APPLAUDING AT THE OLD GUY

2322
01:27:39,020 --> 01:27:40,455
THE OLD DUDE NEVER DIES…

2323
01:27:41,623 --> 01:27:42,457
AMAZED!

2324
01:27:42,991 --> 01:27:43,925
MAN!

2325
01:27:44,259 --> 01:27:45,426
THIS IS THE REAL DEAL

2326
01:27:45,627 --> 01:27:47,428
A ROUND BETWEEN TWO ITALIAN CHEFS

2327
01:27:47,595 --> 01:27:48,429
AN EMERGENCY ALREADY?

2328
01:27:48,496 --> 01:27:49,330
Who turned off the oven?

2329
01:27:49,397 --> 01:27:51,566
-Maybe Chef Canine.
-I think he's possessed by evil.

2330
01:27:51,633 --> 01:27:53,468
He asked me for the circuit box.

2331
01:27:53,534 --> 01:27:55,036
No. Yes.

2332
01:27:55,103 --> 01:27:56,170
He asked me too.

2333
01:27:56,237 --> 01:27:58,706
"Do you think I can
cut the wire with my canine?"

2334
01:27:59,307 --> 01:28:00,608
Do you see this, Jee Seok-jin?

2335
01:28:00,875 --> 01:28:01,776
MISTAKE OVER THE LINE

2336
01:28:01,843 --> 01:28:03,311
Jee Seok-jin isn't here!

2337
01:28:03,511 --> 01:28:04,946
CAN HE SAVE HIMSELF FROM THE MISTAKE?

2338
01:28:08,449 --> 01:28:10,451
Does your husband
look similar to Seok-jin?

2339
01:28:10,518 --> 01:28:11,886
He said he looked like Jee Seok-jin.

2340
01:28:11,953 --> 01:28:14,589
-Jee Seok-jin?
-Jee Seok-jin?

2341
01:28:24,165 --> 01:28:28,936
Subtitle translation by:
Eunsook Youn
